 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence uses a semicolon appropriately?','The index was complete; the date column still needed correction.',['The index was complete; because the date column still needed correction.','The index; was complete and the date column needed correction.','The index was; complete the date column still needed correction.'],'A semicolon can join two closely related independent clauses.','clause-boundary','semicolon-fragment'],
 ['cse-grammar-application','Choose the sentence whose pronoun agrees with its antecedent.','Every applicant must bring the identification card assigned to that applicant.',['Every applicant must bring their identification card assigned to themself.','Each applicants must bring his card.','All applicant brings its card.'],'The revision uses a clear singular antecedent and avoids an agreement mismatch.','pronoun-agreement','antecedent-number-mismatch'],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','A report first states that delayed signatures caused a backlog, then gives a count of affected files. Which transition best introduces that count?','For example,',['Nevertheless,','In contrast,','On the other hand,'],'A count illustrates or supports the preceding claim; it is not a contrast.','evidence-transition','contrast-for-example'],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','A short analysis must present a finding, supporting detail, and limitation. Which order is clearest?','Finding → relevant evidence → limitation on interpretation.',['Limitation → unrelated detail → finding.','Evidence list → recommendation with no stated finding.','Recommendation → limitation → unrelated opening.'],'The sequence lets readers understand the claim, its support, and its boundary.','claim-evidence-limit','evidence-without-claim'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A memo calls the first count provisional and says duplicate entries are still being checked. What does provisional most nearly mean here?','subject to revision after verification',['deliberately false','final and binding','unrelated to the duplicate check'],'The pending duplicate review indicates the count is not final.','provisional-context','provisional-as-false'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A notice says a request is “subject to validation”; the clerk has not yet checked the source record. What follows?','the request has not yet passed the stated validation step',['the request has been rejected permanently','validation is optional','the phrase guarantees approval'],'Subject to validation signals a condition, not an outcome already reached.','conditional-wording','condition-as-result'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','The audit describes a difference as “material” because it changes the eligibility total. In this context, material means:','significant to the decision',['made of physical substance','temporary and harmless','deliberately concealed'],'The stated effect on eligibility makes the difference decision-significant.','contextual-word-meaning','literal-sense-substitution'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','The reviewer says the evidence is “corroborative,” noting that it independently matches the signed log. What role does it play?','it provides additional support for the account',['it replaces all other evidence automatically','it contradicts the log','it proves intent without further facts'],'Independent agreement with the log supports the account; it does not establish every possible claim.','evidence-vocabulary','support-as-proof'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A service change produced a favorable result in one office, but the report says staffing and demand also changed. Which inference is best?','the result is observed, but the effect of the service change alone is uncertain',['the service change caused the entire result','the observation is necessarily false','staffing and demand cannot matter'],'Several simultaneous changes prevent isolating a single cause.','causal-inference-language','association-as-causation'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','The schedule is “contingent on” funding approval, which has not occurred. What is the most accurate reading?','the schedule depends on an unmet condition',['the schedule is forbidden in all cases','funding approval is merely decorative','the schedule has already taken effect'],'Contingent on indicates dependence; the specified approval remains pending.','conditional-wording','condition-ignored'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A report says a pattern is “consistent with” a hypothesis but also notes that other explanations remain. What does the phrase support?','compatibility, not exclusive proof',['certainty that the hypothesis is true','proof that alternatives are impossible','a conclusion unrelated to the data'],'Consistency means the observation fits, while the stated alternatives limit certainty.','qualification-reading','compatibility-as-proof'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','In a notice, “The filing deadline is extended pending system restoration.” Pending most nearly means:','until the stated event is resolved',['because the system has permanently failed','after the deadline has passed','unrelated to restoration'],'Pending marks an interim condition awaiting resolution.','contextual-vocabulary','pending-as-after'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','A review calls the proposed sample “representative” only after comparing its composition with the service population. Representative means:','adequately reflecting relevant features of that population',['containing every member of the population','selected only from the largest office','guaranteeing a correct conclusion'],'The comparison of composition is what supports representativeness; it does not require a census.','contextual-vocabulary','representative-as-complete'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','A report says two measures are “not commensurable” because one counts cases and the other measures elapsed time. Commensurable means:','suitable for direct comparison on a common basis',['numerically identical','collected at the same time only','free from measurement error'],'Different kinds of measures cannot be directly compared without a common basis.','contextual-vocabulary','different-units-as-comparable'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','A reviewer asks for a “succinct” summary that preserves the key finding. Succinct means:','brief and clearly expressed',['short but omitting the main point','highly technical','written before evidence is checked'],'Succinct describes concise expression, not missing substance.','contextual-vocabulary','concise-as-incomplete'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','An instruction says the reviewer must “reconcile” two totals before release. Reconcile means:','identify and resolve the difference between them',['average the totals without investigation','choose the larger total','delete both entries'],'The task is to account for the discrepancy so the records agree for a reason.','contextual-vocabulary','difference-hidden-by-average'],
];
foreach($grammarItems as $r)$add(['concept'=>$r[0],'stem'=>$r[1],'answer'=>$r[2],'wrong'=>$r[3],'why'=>$r[4],'family'=>$r[5],'misconception'=>$r[6],'depth'=>3]);

$filipinoItems=[
 ['masinop','Sa ulat, pinuri ang kawani dahil maingat siya sa paggamit at pag-iingat ng mga kagamitan. Aling kahulugan ng “masinop” ang pinakamalapit?','matipid at maingat sa paggamit',['magastos at pabaya','mabilis ngunit walang ingat','tahimik at nag-iisa'],'Ayon sa gamit ng salita, tumutukoy ang masinop sa maingat at matipid na pangangasiwa.'],
 ['kawani','Ang “kawani” na lumagda sa talaan ay nagtatrabaho sa tanggapan. Ano ang kahulugan nito?','empleyado o tauhan',['kliyente ng tanggapan','gusaling pampamahalaan','dokumentong nilagdaan'],'Ang kawani ay taong nagtatrabaho sa isang tanggapan o pagawaan.'],
 ['salungat','Salungat sa nakasaad na tuntunin ang mungkahing ito. Ano ang ibig sabihin ng “salungat”?','kabaligtaran o hindi naaayon',['kapareho at umaayon','bahagyang kulang','hindi pa nababasa'],'Ang pahayag na salungat ay sumasalungat o hindi umaayon sa tuntunin.'],
 ['makatwiran','Makatwiran ang pasya dahil ipinakita ang batayan at pantay na inilapat ang tuntunin. Ano ang ibig sabihin ng “makatwiran”?','may sapat na dahilan at makatarungang batayan',['padalus-dalos at walang paliwanag','pabor lamang sa kakilala','lihim at hindi masusuri'],'Inilalarawan ng konteksto ang pasyang may maipapaliwanag na batayan.'],
 ['hinuha','Hindi tahasang sinabi sa ulat ang sanhi; kailangang gumawa ng hinuha mula sa mga palatandaan. Ang hinuha ay:','konklusyong nabuo mula sa ebidensiya',['direktang sipi lamang','petsa ng pagkakalathala','utos na walang batayan'],'Ang hinuha ay konklusyong iniisip mula sa ibinigay na palatandaan o ebidensiya.'],
 ['pabatid','Naglabas ang tanggapan ng pabatid tungkol sa bagong oras ng serbisyo. Ano ang pabatid?','abiso o opisyal na impormasyon',['lihim na rekord','resibo ng bayad','listahan ng parusa'],'Ang pabatid ay impormasyong ipinapaalam sa mga kinauukulan.'],
 ['paglilinaw','Humingi ang tagasuri ng paglilinaw dahil maaaring unawain sa dalawang paraan ang pangungusap. Ano ang layunin nito?','gawing malinaw ang kahulugan',['baguhin ang lahat ng datos','alisin ang ebidensiya','ipagpaliban ang pasya nang walang dahilan'],'Nililinaw ang pahayag upang matukoy ang nilalayong kahulugan.'],
 ['mapanagot','Dapat mapanagot ang opisyal matapos ang patas na pagsusuri ng ebidensiya. Ang “mapanagot” ay nangangahulugang:','maharap sa pananagutan ayon sa naaangkop na proseso',['parusahan bago siyasatin','palitan ang lahat ng kawani','itago ang pagkakamali'],'Ang pananagutan ay sinusunod sa naaangkop na proseso at batay sa ebidensiya.'],
 ['napapanahon','Napapanahon ang tala dahil regular itong ina-update. Ano ang kahulugan ng “napapanahon”?','bago o angkop sa kasalukuyang panahon',['laging tama kahit hindi beripikado','nakatago sa lumang lalagyan','naisulat nang sabay-sabay'],'Ipinahihiwatig ng regular na pag-update na kasalukuyan ang tala.'],
 ['masalimuot','Masalimuot ang proseso sapagkat maraming hakbang at magkakaugnay na dokumento. Ang ibig sabihin nito ay:','komplikado at maraming bahagi',['maikli at payak','walang kaugnayan sa dokumento','mabilis matapos palagi'],'Ang maraming magkakaugnay na hakbang ang dahilan kung bakit komplikado ang proseso.'],
 ['maaasahan','Maaasahan ang bilang sapagkat naitugma ito sa dalawang hiwalay na talaan. Ano ang ibig sabihin ng “maaasahan”?','mapagkakatiwalaan batay sa pagsusuri',['tiyak na walang pagkakamali magpakailanman','mas mataas kaysa sa ibang bilang','hindi maaaring suriin muli'],'Ang pagtutugma sa magkahiwalay na tala ay nagbibigay ng batayan para pagkatiwalaan ang bilang, hindi garantiya ng kawalang-mali.'],
 ['pagkiling','Sinuri ang pagkiling sa survey dahil iisang pangkat lamang ang sumagot. Ano ang tinutukoy ng “pagkiling”?','sistematikong paglihis sa paraan ng pagpili o pagsukat',['random na pag-aayos ng papel','pagiging eksakto ng orasan','pagkakaiba ng dalawang font'],'Maaaring maimpluwensiyahan ng iisang pangkat ng sumagot ang resulta.'],
];
foreach($filipinoItems as $r)$add(['concept'=>'cse-filipino-word-usage','stem'=>$r[1],'answer'=>$r[2],'wrong'=>$r[3],'why'=>$r[4],'family'=>'filipino-contextual-vocabulary','misconception'=>'literal-or-overbroad-meaning','depth'=>3]);

$passages=[
 ['A district office introduced a checklist for applications. Returned files decreased during the next month, but the report did not record whether applicants used each checklist item or whether staffing changed.','What does the report establish most directly?','Returned files decreased during the observed month.',['The checklist alone caused the decrease.','Every applicant followed the checklist.','Staffing had no effect.'],'The count changed, while checklist use and staffing were not controlled.','reading-observed-vs-causal','causal-overclaim'],
 ['A library extended its service hours for six weeks. Visits after work increased, while morning visits stayed similar. The library has not yet compared costs or surveyed visitors who did not attend.','Which conclusion is best supported?','The new hours coincided with more after-work visits, but overall access effects remain incomplete.',['The schedule is cost-effective for every branch.','Morning visitors were displaced.','The change caused all attendance differences.'],'The passage reports one group’s increase and identifies missing evidence about cost and nonusers.','reading-scope-of-evidence','one-subgroup-as-total'],
 ['A records team compared paper and digital retrieval. Digital searches were faster for indexed files; unindexed files took longer because staff had to locate the source folder first.','What distinction explains the mixed results?','Indexing status changed the retrieval task.',['Digital access was always slower.','Paper files were never searchable.','The comparison proves all records should be digitized.'],'The results differ by whether an index exists; the passage does not support a universal conclusion.','reading-condition-comparison','average-hides-subgroup'],
 ['A public notice was translated into two languages. More people requested clarification, but the office also moved the notice to a more visible location that week.','What should an analyst avoid claiming?','That translation alone caused the increase in inquiries.',['That inquiries increased.','That visibility may be relevant.','That the timing of both changes should be recorded.'],'The two simultaneous changes make isolated causal attribution uncertain.','reading-confounding','single-change-attribution'],
 ['A survey found high satisfaction among people who completed an online form. The response rate was low, and paper users were not invited to respond.','What is the main limitation?','The respondents may not represent all service users.',['The respondents were necessarily dissatisfied.','A low response rate proves the form failed.','Online responses cannot contain useful information.'],'Nonresponse and channel exclusion limit generalization; they do not erase the answers received.','reading-sampling-limit','sample-equals-population'],
 ['A team reported that missed appointments fell after reminders began. During the same period, the office shortened the waiting time for appointments.','Which additional information would best help interpret the change?','Whether appointment availability or the user mix also changed.',['The color of the reminder envelope.','Whether the office name changed.','Whether all reminders used the same font.'],'A relevant alternative change could account for some of the observed decline.','reading-alternative-explanation','irrelevant-detail'],
 ['A report compares two service centers using total cases completed. One center operated for five days; the other operated for eight.','Which comparison would be more informative about pace?','Cases completed per operating day.',['Total cases alone.','Number of signs at each center.','The center with more days must be faster.'],'A rate adjusts for the unequal operating time.','reading-denominator-choice','total-as-rate'],
 ['An audit found duplicate records in one month. The team corrected the entries and added a validation step, then scheduled another audit to check whether duplicates recur.','Why is the follow-up audit useful?','It tests whether the corrective control works over time.',['It proves the first audit was wrong.','It makes duplicate records impossible by definition.','It replaces the need to document the correction.'],'A later check evaluates whether the control reduces recurrence.','reading-monitoring-purpose','single-check-as-permanent-proof'],
 ['A memo recommends prioritizing urgent requests. It defines urgency by a deadline within 48 hours and requires the date to be verified from the original notice.','Which request qualifies on the stated rule?','A verified notice shows a deadline 36 hours away.',['A requester says the matter feels urgent but gives no deadline.','A verified notice shows a deadline in 72 hours.','A file is old but has no due date.'],'Only the first example meets the stated time threshold with verified evidence.','reading-rule-application','urgency-by-feeling'],
 ['A pilot used a new queue number system in one office. Average waiting time fell, although the office did not record the distribution of waits or compare peak and off-peak periods.','What important detail remains unknown?','Whether the improvement was similar across times and users.',['Whether average waiting time was measured.','Whether the office had a queue.','Whether the number system existed.'],'The overall average can mask variation across periods or groups.','reading-aggregate-limits','average-as-uniform'],
 ['Two reports list different totals because one includes pending cases and the other counts only completed cases.','What should be checked before comparing the totals?','Whether both reports use the same inclusion definition.',['Which report has the longer title.','Whether the totals are printed in bold.','Whether pending cases are always completed.'],'Different definitions make the totals noncomparable until aligned.','reading-measure-definition','unlike-measures-compared'],
 ['A department says complaints fell after it opened a second channel for reporting. The new channel records complaints separately, and the published figure includes only the original channel.','What interpretation is most cautious?','The published count may not capture complaints across both channels.',['Complaints definitely fell in total.','The new channel received no complaints.','The second channel cannot affect measurement.'],'The reported measure excludes a channel, so it may not represent total complaints.','reading-measurement-coverage','missing-channel-ignored'],
 ['A summary claims that all applicants understood a form because 18 of 20 interviewed applicants said it was clear. The interviews were conducted at one urban site.','Which revision is most responsible?','Most interviewed applicants at that site found it clear; broader understanding needs more evidence.',['All applicants nationwide understood the form.','The interviews prove nobody had difficulty.','The result should be discarded entirely.'],'The conclusion should match the sample and location.','reading-qualified-conclusion','sample-overgeneralization'],
 ['A team reports both the number of files corrected and the proportion corrected. The count rose, while the proportion declined because the total number of files rose faster.','How can both statements be true?','The numerator increased, but the denominator increased more quickly.',['A proportion never depends on the total.','The count must have been recorded incorrectly.','A rising count always means a rising rate.'],'A rate can fall despite a rising numerator if the base grows faster.','reading-rate-vs-count','count-rate-confusion'],
 ['A data report gives a rate but omits how the denominator was defined.','What is the best next step before comparing the rate with another report?','Check the population and denominator definitions used for both rates.',['Compare the percentages without checking their bases.','Assume both reports count the same population.','Replace the figures with an overall total.'],'Rates are comparable only when their populations and denominator definitions are sufficiently aligned.','reading-contextual-source-use','denominator-definition-ignored'],
];
foreach($passages as $i=>$r){$concepts=['cse-reading-comprehension','cse-contextual-inference','cse-evidence-strength','cse-data-interpretation'];$concept=$concepts[$i%count($concepts)];$add(['concept'=>$concept,'stem'=>'Read the short report: “'.$r[0].'” '.$r[1],'answer'=>$r[2],'wrong'=>$r[3],'why'=>$r[4],'family'=>$r[5],'misconception'=>$r[6],'depth'=>4]);}

/* GENERAL INFORMATION: scoped civic/law application, tied to primary texts and live review. */
$giCases=[
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A citizen asks why an agency must explain how it used a public fund. Which constitutional principle most directly supports public accountability?','Public office is a public trust.',['Public office is private property.','Only elected officials are accountable.','A public fund is exempt from review.'],'Article XI, Section 1 treats public office as a public trust and requires public officers and employees to be accountable to the people.','1987-philippine-constitution','public-trust-accountability'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A civic group argues that government authority ultimately comes from the people. Which constitutional statement supports this?','Sovereignty resides in the people and all government authority emanates from them.',['Government authority originates only in agencies.','Sovereignty belongs to a single branch.','Public authority is inherited by officeholders.'],'Article II, Section 1 locates sovereignty in the people and government authority in that source.','1987-philippine-constitution','popular-sovereignty'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A bill has passed both houses of Congress and is presented for approval or veto. Which branch is acting on it at this stage?','The executive branch, through the President.',['The judiciary, by deciding constitutionality automatically.','The Commission on Audit, by enacting the bill.','A local council, by signing national legislation.'],'Congress exercises legislative power; presentment for approval or veto is an executive function under the Constitution.','1987-philippine-constitution','branch-function-confusion'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A court resolves a justiciable dispute by interpreting the law and applying it to the case. This is principally an exercise of:','judicial power',['legislative power','the power to appropriate funds','administrative rulemaking by Congress'],'Article VIII vests judicial power in the courts, including settling actual controversies involving legally demandable rights.','1987-philippine-constitution','judicial-legislative-confusion'],
 ['cse-government-functions','Congress considers a measure to establish a national policy. Which constitutional branch primarily exercises legislative power?','Congress, consisting of the Senate and House of Representatives.',['The Supreme Court alone.','The President’s Cabinet alone.','The Commission on Elections.'],'Article VI vests legislative power in Congress, subject to constitutional processes.','1987-philippine-constitution','branch-role-confusion'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','Officers search a private home without a warrant and without facts establishing a recognized exception. Which right is most directly implicated?','The protection against unreasonable searches and seizures.',['The right to a speedy trial only.','The right to form an association only.','The prohibition on impairment of contracts only.'],'Article III, Section 2 protects persons and houses against unreasonable searches and seizures; the item supplies no exception facts.','1987-philippine-constitution','search-authority-assumed'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is deprived of liberty without notice or a meaningful opportunity to be heard in a proceeding where process is required. Which protection is implicated?','Due process of law.',['The right to a particular office.','The right to automatic acquittal.','The privilege of legislative immunity.'],'Article III, Section 1 protects against deprivation of life, liberty, or property without due process of law.','1987-philippine-constitution','due-process-as-outcome'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A peaceful assembly criticizes a government policy. Which Bill of Rights protection is most directly relevant?','Freedom of speech and peaceful assembly.',['An unconditional right to enter any private property.','A guarantee that criticism changes policy.','An exemption from every generally applicable law.'],'Article III, Section 4 protects speech, expression, and peaceful assembly, subject to lawful constitutional limits.','1987-philippine-constitution','rights-as-absolute-outcome'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person under custodial investigation asks for counsel. Which constitutional safeguard is relevant?','The right to be informed of the right to remain silent and to have competent and independent counsel.',['A right to choose the investigating officer.','A guarantee that no question may ever be asked.','A right to automatic release in every case.'],'Article III, Section 12 specifies safeguards during custodial investigation, including counsel.','1987-philippine-constitution','custodial-right-overclaim'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A public service policy excludes a group from a benefit solely because of a protected personal characteristic, without a lawful basis. Which general principle is most relevant?','Equal protection and respect for human dignity.',['Public convenience always overrides individual rights.','Equal protection applies only to property.','A policy is fair whenever it is written.'],'The Constitution protects equal protection; the UDHR also affirms equality and dignity. Specific legality depends on the controlling rule and facts.','1987-philippine-constitution','formal-rule-equals-fairness'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A report alleges degrading treatment but provides no independent verification. What is the most responsible public-information response?','Treat the allegation seriously, protect affected persons, and verify facts through appropriate procedures.',['Publish the allegation as proven immediately.','Dismiss it because no conclusion is yet final.','Identify the complainant publicly without consent.'],'Human dignity warrants serious attention while fairness and reliable verification prohibit presenting an unverified claim as established fact.','universal-declaration-human-rights','allegation-as-finding'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','Residents submit comments during a consultation, but the agency has not yet evaluated them. What can be concluded?','The comments are inputs for consideration; their submission alone does not determine the final decision.',['Every comment must be adopted.','Participation is meaningless unless the proposal changes.','The agency may disregard every applicable procedure.'],'Participation contributes information and views; the stated facts do not require adopting each comment.','1987-philippine-constitution','participation-as-veto'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A clerk discovers that a published service statistic excluded a category of completed requests. What is the accountable next step?','Correct or qualify the report and preserve the basis for the revision.',['Leave the statistic unchanged to avoid questions.','Delete the source records.','Replace it with an estimate without disclosure.'],'Public accountability requires accurate, reviewable reporting rather than concealing a material limitation.','republic-act-6713','error-concealment'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A supplier offers an expensive personal gift to an employee handling its application. Which response best follows public-service ethics?','Decline or report the offer under applicable rules and avoid compromising impartiality.',['Accept it if no payment is requested.','Accept it after the decision is made, regardless of policy.','Keep it secret if the application is approved.'],'RA 6713 requires public-interest-oriented conduct and addresses gifts and conflicts; the employee should follow applicable reporting procedures.','republic-act-6713','gift-after-decision'],
 ['cse-conflict-of-interest','An employee is assigned to evaluate a proposal submitted by a close relative’s business. What is the prudent first action?','Disclose the relationship and follow the applicable recusal or conflict procedure.',['Continue without disclosure if the scoring is objective.','Alter the criteria to favor the relative.','Ask the relative to submit under another name.'],'Disclosure lets the agency manage the conflict and protect impartiality; exact recusal steps follow governing rules.','republic-act-6713','conflict-only-if-biased'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee receives a request from a political supporter and a similar request from another citizen. What response best reflects political neutrality?','Apply the same lawful criteria to both requests.',['Prioritize the supporter because the request is familiar.','Refuse the second request without review.','Change the criteria after learning the requester’s affiliation.'],'RA 6713 includes political neutrality among the norms of conduct; service decisions should not be based on partisan preference.','republic-act-6713','partisan-preference'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public employee is asked to use office time and equipment for a private commercial task. Which principle is most directly implicated?','Commitment to public interest and proper use of public resources.',['A right to use public resources for any personal project.','A rule that private activity always takes priority.','A requirement to destroy the work record.'],'Public resources and working time are entrusted for public functions; private use must follow applicable rules.','republic-act-6713','public-resource-private-use'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A citizen writes to a public office about a matter within its authority. Under RA 6713, what is the general response-time duty stated for written communications?','Respond within 15 working days from receipt.',['Respond within 15 calendar months.','Respond only after the next election.','No response is required for written communications.'],'RA 6713, Section 5(a), directs public officials and employees to respond to letters and other communications within 15 working days from receipt, subject to its terms.','republic-act-6713','calendar-vs-working-days'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A program’s report counts only applicants who completed the final step, although the question concerns access at the first step. What should a reviewer flag?','The measure may omit people who encountered barriers earlier in the process.',['The omitted group must have completed the process.','The final-step count measures every access barrier.','The measure is invalid only if the number is small.'],'The denominator and point of measurement may exclude people whose access problem occurred before completion.','1987-philippine-constitution','completion-only-coverage'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A local office plans to burn mixed waste in an open area to clear a storage site. Which law is most directly relevant to ecological solid-waste management?','Republic Act No. 9003.',['Republic Act No. 6713 only.','The Civil Code provisions on contracts only.','Republic Act No. 8749 only, regardless of waste type.'],'RA 9003 is the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act; open burning and waste handling must be assessed under applicable environmental rules.','republic-act-9003','waste-law-confusion'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A community proposes source segregation and recovery of recyclable materials before disposal. Which approach is consistent with RA 9003?','Segregate waste at source and use appropriate recovery/management systems.',['Mix all waste and rely only on final disposal.','Treat recyclable materials as outside any management plan.','Burn mixed waste to reduce sorting effort.'],'RA 9003 establishes ecological solid-waste management, including segregation and recovery measures.','republic-act-9003','mixed-waste-default'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A factory’s emissions may affect nearby residents. Which national law is principally concerned with air pollution prevention and control?','Republic Act No. 8749.',['Republic Act No. 9003, which focuses on solid waste.','Republic Act No. 6713, which governs public ethics.','The UDHR alone.'],'RA 8749 is the Philippine Clean Air Act of 1999, addressing air quality management and pollution prevention/control.','republic-act-8749','air-solid-waste-confusion'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A report observes lower smoke readings after a local intervention, but weather and industrial activity also changed. What is the cautious conclusion?','Readings fell, but the intervention’s isolated causal effect is not established.',['The intervention caused the entire change.','The readings prove weather was irrelevant.','No observation should be retained.'],'Concurrent changes confound causal attribution, even though the measured trend can still be reported.','republic-act-8749','trend-as-cause'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is compelled to testify against themself in a criminal proceeding. Which constitutional protection is most directly implicated?','The privilege against being compelled to be a witness against oneself.',['The right to vote in every proceeding.','The right to a particular public office.','The prohibition on unreasonable searches only.'],'Article III, Section 17 protects a person from being compelled to be a witness against themself.','1987-philippine-constitution','self-incrimination-as-required-testimony'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A court reviews whether an official act is within constitutional authority in an actual controversy. Which function is implicated?','Judicial review within the courts’ constitutional role.',['Writing the annual national budget.','Conducting a legislative election.','Issuing an executive appointment.'],'Article VIII includes the courts’ authority to determine grave abuse of discretion in the exercise of government power.','1987-philippine-constitution','review-as-legislation'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A policy affects a natural resource and future generations. Which stated constitutional state policy is relevant?','The State shall protect and advance the right of the people to a balanced and healthful ecology.',['The Constitution excludes environmental policy.','Only private entities may address natural resources.','Environmental concerns may never affect public decisions.'],'Article II, Section 16 states the policy concerning a balanced and healthful ecology.','1987-philippine-constitution','ecology-policy-omitted'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A public institution receives a credible complaint of rights abuse. Which broad constitutional duty is consistent with the State’s role?','Respect and protect human rights, while following lawful fact-finding procedures.',['Treat every complaint as already proven.','Ignore the complaint until a court issues a final ruling.','Publish private identifying details immediately.'],'The Constitution recognizes the State’s respect for human rights; fair investigation distinguishes allegation from finding.','1987-philippine-constitution','rights-vs-fair-process'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A residents’ group requests records to understand a government decision. Which approach best supports informed civic participation?','Provide accessible, nonconfidential records through the applicable lawful process.',['Refuse all records because government work is private.','Release confidential personal data without screening.','Provide an unexplained total with no source information.'],'Access supports informed participation, while lawful confidentiality and privacy limits still apply.','1987-philippine-constitution','access-as-unlimited'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A supervisor asks staff to destroy the original calculation after discovering a reporting error. What should the employee do?','Preserve the record and use authorized correction and reporting procedures.',['Destroy it to make the corrected number the only record.','Change the file date to hide the revision.','Send it to an unauthorized personal account.'],'A defensible correction preserves an audit trail and follows records and reporting rules.','republic-act-6713','audit-trail-destruction'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A citizen’s request is delayed because staff prefer to serve people they know first. Which norm of conduct is most directly relevant?','Justness and sincerity, together with responsiveness to the public.',['Simple living only.','Nationalism only.','Private loyalty over public duty.'],'RA 6713 calls for justness and sincerity and responsiveness; familiarity is not a fair service criterion.','republic-act-6713','favoritism-as-efficiency'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A public notice uses a technical term without explaining who is affected or what action is required. Which improvement best serves the public?','Use accurate plain language and specify the affected group and required step.',['Add more technical terms without explanation.','Remove the deadline and contact details.','Assume every reader already knows the process.'],'Responsiveness and professionalism support clear, usable communication without sacrificing accuracy.','republic-act-6713','complexity-as-precision'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A town proposes a materials recovery facility as part of its local solid-waste plan. What is its general function under RA 9003?','Receive and sort segregated materials for composting, recycling, or other recovery before proper residual disposal.',['Generate electricity from every waste item.','Replace all source segregation.','Serve as a site for open burning.'],'RA 9003 Section 32 places MRFs within the recovery system; a facility complements source segregation and handles materials for recovery and residual management under applicable requirements.','republic-act-9003','facility-as-disposal-only'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A public office plans a project that could affect air quality. Which first step is more responsible than assuming no impact?','Assess the relevant emissions and applicable air-quality requirements.',['Assume a small office project has no emissions.','Wait for complaints before keeping any record.','Use a solid-waste plan as the only air-quality measure.'],'RA 8749 centers on air pollution control; the relevant impacts and regulatory requirements should be identified.','republic-act-8749','no-complaint-no-impact'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A rule is applied consistently, but a group cannot meaningfully access the service because the format is inaccessible. What should the agency examine?','Whether the process provides equal and meaningful access consistent with applicable rights and duties.',['Whether formal consistency alone proves accessibility.','Whether the group should be removed from the count.','Whether all accommodation requests must be denied.'],'Equal treatment in form can still miss an access barrier; the facts call for review under applicable law and policy.','1987-philippine-constitution','formal-equality-suffices'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A citizen asks which body has constitutional power to audit government accounts and expenditures. Which institution is the constitutional Commission on Audit?','The Commission on Audit.',['The Commission on Elections.','The Civil Service Commission.','The Department of Justice.'],'Article IX-D establishes the Commission on Audit and its audit functions.','1987-philippine-constitution','constitutional-commission-confusion'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A government office implements an enacted statute through lawful administration. Which description is most accurate?','Implementation is an executive/administrative function, constrained by the statute and Constitution.',['Implementation lets the office rewrite the statute.','Implementation is exclusively a court function.','The office may disregard statutory limits.'],'The executive branch administers and enforces law; it may not replace legislative authority or constitutional limits.','1987-philippine-constitution','implementation-as-lawmaking'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','An employee notices a possible conflict in a procurement record but is unsure whether it violates a rule. What is the sound first response?','Document the concern and consult the designated ethics or compliance process.',['Alter the record to remove the concern.','Accuse a named person publicly without checking.','Ignore it because uncertainty means no risk.'],'A documented, appropriate review preserves facts and avoids both concealment and unsupported accusation.','republic-act-6713','uncertainty-as-inaction'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A meeting has many comments from one neighborhood and none from another affected area. What should the facilitator note?','The input may not represent all affected communities.',['The most frequent view automatically represents everyone.','The absent neighborhood has no relevant interest.','Comments should be discarded.'],'Participation volume from one group does not prove representativeness of the wider affected population.','1987-philippine-constitution','loudest-group-as-consensus'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public employee is asked to disclose a nonconfidential procedure so applicants can follow it. Which response best aligns with public service?','Provide accurate information through the proper channel and protect only legitimately confidential material.',['Refuse all information to preserve convenience.','Release unrelated personal records too.','Give different instructions to favored applicants.'],'Responsiveness and accountability support accessible procedure information while respecting lawful confidentiality.','republic-act-6713','all-or-nothing-disclosure'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Under RA 9003 Section 22, what is a minimum storage practice for segregated solid waste pending collection?','Use a separate container for each waste type and identify it with the applicable category.',['Mix all types in one unmarked container.','Label every container “residual” regardless of its contents.','Store recyclables only after they have been mixed with other waste.'],'Section 22 requires separate containers for each type and appropriate labels such as compostable, non-recyclable, recyclable, or special waste.','ra9003-storage-labels','same-container-for-all-types'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A city records air-quality readings at only one roadside location and uses them to describe the entire region. What limitation should be considered?','The measurement location may not represent conditions across the region.',['One reading is necessarily false.','Location cannot affect air measurements.','A regional claim needs no coverage information.'],'Measurement coverage and location affect how widely a local observation can be generalized.','republic-act-8749','single-site-as-region'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A law imposes a penalty for conduct that was not an offense when done. Which constitutional protection is most directly implicated?','The prohibition on ex post facto laws.',['The right to form a corporation.','The guarantee of a public subsidy.','The right to a particular job.'],'Article III, Section 22 prohibits ex post facto laws and bills of attainder.','1987-philippine-constitution','retroactivity-confusion'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is held solely because of political beliefs and aspirations, without lawful charge. Which protection is relevant?','The Constitution prohibits detention solely by reason of political beliefs and aspirations.',['Political belief automatically establishes guilt.','Every detention is lawful if administrative.','Only property rights are implicated.'],'Article III, Section 18 expressly addresses detention solely by reason of political beliefs and aspirations.','1987-philippine-constitution','belief-as-ground'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A service rule is challenged as discriminatory. What information is most useful before drawing a conclusion?','The rule’s text, purpose, affected groups, actual operation, and applicable legal standards.',['Only the office’s stated intention.','Only one anecdote.','The number of pages in the rule.'],'A fair assessment needs the governing standard and relevant facts; intention alone does not resolve impact or legality.','universal-declaration-human-rights','intent-alone-decides'],
 ['cse-public-interest','An employee processes a request involving public information and personal data. Which approach is best?','Apply the lawful disclosure basis and data-privacy principles, releasing appropriate records while protecting data that must remain confidential.',['Release every identifier because the request is public.','Withhold all information automatically because it contains personal data.','Post the unredacted records on a public website.'],'RA 10173 protects personal data but does not bar every public disclosure; apply lawful authority and the transparency, legitimate-purpose, and proportionality principles.','1987-philippine-constitution','public-records-as-unrestricted'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee is invited to use nonpublic information learned at work for a private advantage. Which response best follows public-service ethics?','Do not use the information for private gain; report or seek guidance under applicable rules.',['Use it if no written contract prohibits it.','Share it only with friends.','Alter the official record first.'],'Public office is held in trust; misuse of nonpublic official information undermines impartial public service and may violate applicable rules.','republic-act-6713','information-as-personal-asset'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A manager wants to report a success rate but leaves out the number of cases that failed. Which improvement is most informative?','Report the numerator, denominator, period, and relevant inclusion rule.',['Report only the favorable percentage.','Remove the period so the statistic looks stable.','Compare it with an unrelated measure.'],'Readers need the base and measurement definition to interpret a rate and assess completeness.','republic-act-6713','selective-reporting'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Under RA 9003 Section 10, which collection responsibility is assigned at the barangay level?','Segregation and collection of biodegradable, compostable, and reusable wastes.',['Collection of non-recyclable and special wastes, which the section assigns to the city or municipality.','Final operation of every national sanitary landfill.','Setting air-emission limits for industrial sources.'],'Section 10 assigns segregation and collection of biodegradable, compostable, and reusable wastes at barangay level; the city or municipality is responsible for non-recyclable and special wastes.','ra9003-local-collection-responsibility','barangay-municipal-duty-reversal'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A proposed activity may emit pollutants; an employee claims it is compliant because no odor is detectable. What is the flaw?','Absence of a noticeable odor alone does not establish compliance with air-quality requirements.',['Odor is the only legally relevant measurement.','Every pollutant is detectable by smell.','A lack of complaint proves compliance.'],'RA 8749 compliance depends on applicable standards and evidence, not merely subjective odor detection.','republic-act-8749','sensory-test-as-compliance'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A national commission established by the Constitution exercises its independent constitutional mandate. What should an analyst avoid assuming?','That it is simply a department under one of the three traditional branches.',['That constitutional bodies have legal powers.','That its mandate has defined limits.','That its actions may be reviewed under applicable law.'],'The Constitution establishes independent constitutional commissions; their placement and powers should not be conflated with ordinary departments.','1987-philippine-constitution','commission-as-department'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A policy asks for feedback through both online and in-person channels. Why can the two channels matter?','They may reach people with different access conditions and participation barriers.',['Every channel reaches identical users.','More channels automatically guarantee equal influence.','Online feedback should replace every other form.'],'Multiple channels can reduce some access barriers, but representation and influence still require evaluation.','1987-philippine-constitution','channel-count-as-equity'],
];
