$giMore=[
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public employee is asked to expedite an application because the requester is a political ally. What action is most consistent with political neutrality?','Use the same lawful queue and criteria applied to comparable applicants.',['Move the ally ahead without recording the reason.','Reject the application because of the requester’s affiliation.','Change the eligibility rule for that applicant.'],'RA 6713 identifies political neutrality as a norm; comparable cases should be treated under the same applicable criteria.','republic-act-6713','political-favor'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public official receives a routine letter within the office’s authority. Which practice is consistent with the statutory duty to respond?','Acknowledge and respond within the statutory period, ordinarily 15 working days from receipt.',['Wait 15 calendar months.','Respond only if the writer is personally known.','Delete the letter if no form was attached.'],'RA 6713, Section 5(a), states the 15-working-day response requirement for letters and other communications.','republic-act-6713','working-days-misread'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A report is corrected after an error is found. Which recordkeeping practice best supports accountability?','Retain the original, document the correction and reason, and identify the corrected version.',['Erase the original without a trace.','Change the date to make the correction appear original.','Circulate the corrected total without noting the change.'],'A transparent correction preserves provenance so the adjustment can be examined.','republic-act-6713','silent-correction'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee with access to confidential bid evaluations is asked by a friend to share scores before the official release. What is the proper response?','Protect the confidential information and use only the authorized disclosure process.',['Share the scores because the friend promises not to circulate them.','Give an unofficial hint without sending the document.','Post the scores anonymously.'],'RA 6713 prohibits using or disclosing confidential information to further private interests or prejudice the public interest.','republic-act-6713','confidential-information-as-favor'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A staff member can answer a citizen’s question but is unsure about one detail. What is the most professional response?','Give the verified information and identify or check the uncertain detail before stating it as fact.',['Guess to avoid a delay.','Refuse to provide any information.','Invent a standard answer.'],'Responsiveness does not justify misinformation; verify uncertain facts and communicate the limit.','republic-act-6713','speed-over-accuracy'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A dashboard reports “90% resolved” but does not define whether reopened cases count. What should be clarified?','The numerator, denominator, period, and treatment of reopened cases.',['The dashboard color palette.','The employee who designed the chart.','The figure should be rounded to 100%.'],'Operational definitions are necessary to interpret a performance measure.','republic-act-6713','undefined-metric'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A public office has a service rule that is lawful but difficult to understand. What response best reflects responsiveness?','Explain the rule in clear language while preserving its actual requirements.',['Omit requirements so the process sounds easy.','Give different explanations to different applicants.','Replace the rule with a personal preference.'],'Clear explanation supports responsive service without misrepresenting controlling requirements.','republic-act-6713','plain-language-as-rule-change'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A consultation receives feedback from a group that may be directly affected but is absent from the meeting. What is a useful next step?','Use an accessible channel to seek that group’s input before characterizing the feedback as representative.',['Assume the attendees represent every affected person.','Treat nonattendance as consent.','Exclude the group from future analysis.'],'The participant set may not represent all affected interests; further accessible input can address the coverage gap.','1987-philippine-constitution','nonattendance-as-consent'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A proposed restriction affects expression. What should a reviewer do before declaring it valid or invalid?','Identify the precise rule, governmental purpose, facts, and controlling constitutional standard.',['Assume every restriction is valid.','Assume every restriction is invalid without reviewing its basis.','Decide only from the speaker’s popularity.'],'The Constitution protects expression, but applying it requires the governing standard and specific facts.','1987-philippine-constitution','absolute-right-assumption'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is prosecuted twice for the same offense after a valid acquittal, with no stated exception. Which protection is implicated?','The protection against double jeopardy.',['The right to a particular public office.','The right to a government subsidy.','The prohibition on unreasonable searches only.'],'Article III, Section 21 protects against being twice put in jeopardy of punishment for the same offense.','1987-philippine-constitution','repeat-case-confusion'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is charged with an offense but is not informed of its nature and cause. Which right is most directly implicated?','The right of the accused to be informed of the nature and cause of the accusation.',['The right to vote in every proceeding.','The right to select a judge.','A right to avoid every trial.'],'Article III, Section 14 includes the right to be informed of the nature and cause of the accusation.','1987-philippine-constitution','notice-as-verdict'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A government office uses a public fund for a purpose not authorized by law. Which principle is most relevant?','Public funds must be spent under lawful authority and remain subject to accountability.',['An office may use funds for any useful purpose.','A public fund becomes private once assigned.','Only private contributions are reviewable.'],'Public office is a public trust, and public expenditure must follow legal authorization and audit requirements.','1987-philippine-constitution','usefulness-as-authorization'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A bill that raises revenue is introduced in Congress. In which chamber must it originate under the Constitution?','The House of Representatives.',['The Senate only.','The Supreme Court.','The Commission on Audit.'],'Article VI, Section 24 requires revenue bills to originate exclusively in the House, while the Senate may propose or concur with amendments.','1987-philippine-constitution','bill-origin-chamber'],
 ['cse-government-functions','A dispute concerns the constitutionality of a government action in an actual case. Which institution can exercise judicial review?','The courts, within the constitutional requirements for judicial review.',['A records clerk acting without a case.','Any private organization by issuing a binding judgment.','The legislature by deciding a pending court case.'],'Judicial review belongs to the courts in cases meeting constitutional and justiciability requirements.','1987-philippine-constitution','review-without-case'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Under RA 9003 Section 21, segregation should primarily occur at the point of origin for which sources?','Household, institutional, industrial, commercial, and agricultural sources.',['Households only.','Commercial establishments only.','Disposal facilities only, after collection.'],'Section 21 includes household, institutional, industrial, commercial, and agricultural sources in mandatory source segregation.','ra9003-covered-source-types','household-only-scope'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A local plan identifies waste reduction, reuse, recycling, and responsible disposal. What is its strongest feature under the ecological approach?','It treats waste management as an integrated sequence rather than disposal alone.',['It relies on open burning as the default.','It ignores waste generation.','It treats every material as nonrecoverable.'],'RA 9003’s framework covers reduction, reuse, recycling, recovery, and appropriate residual management.','republic-act-9003','disposal-only-model'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A facility proposes an emissions-control measure. Which evidence would be most relevant to whether it works?','Comparable air-quality or emissions measurements before and after, with conditions documented.',['A public-relations slogan.','The number of employees at the facility.','A photograph with no date or measurement.'],'Air-quality evaluation needs relevant measurements and context; a slogan or unrelated observation cannot establish effectiveness.','republic-act-8749','claim-as-measurement'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A monitoring station is moved closer to a road and readings rise. What should the analyst check?','Whether location or monitoring conditions changed before interpreting the trend.',['Whether the new station has a shorter name.','Whether all readings should be discarded.','Whether road traffic is unrelated by definition.'],'A changed measurement location can affect comparability, even when the readings remain useful.','republic-act-8749','measurement-change-ignored'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A public-facing procedure requires an unnecessary disclosure of sensitive personal information. What should the reviewing office examine?','Whether the information is necessary and lawfully collected for the stated purpose.',['Whether more personal data always improves service.','Whether the data can be posted publicly.','Whether a verbal request replaces every safeguard.'],'Respect for dignity and privacy calls for a lawful, purpose-related basis; the facts do not justify blanket collection.','1987-philippine-constitution','more-data-is-better'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A citizen asks for a nonconfidential record that explains a decision. What is the best initial approach?','Locate the record and apply the applicable access and privacy rules.',['Refuse automatically because it is a government record.','Release unrelated personal data with it.','Create a new record and label it original.'],'The request calls for a lawful access review, distinguishing releasable material from protected data.','1987-philippine-constitution','blanket-release-or-refusal'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee is offered a benefit by a person whose request the employee can influence. What should guide the employee?','Applicable gift and conflict rules, public-interest duties, and disclosure procedures.',['The employee’s personal view that the benefit is harmless.','Whether the benefit is kept off the record.','Whether the requester promises future support.'],'RA 6713 addresses gifts and public-service norms; the employee should use the controlling rules, not personal assurances.','republic-act-6713','private-assessment-controls'],
 ['cse-public-interest','An office uses one queue for citizens and a separate unrecorded queue for acquaintances. Which concern is strongest?','Unequal treatment and lack of transparent, reviewable service criteria.',['The queue numbers may be printed in a different font.','Every separate queue is inherently unlawful.','Acquaintances should always be served last.'],'The key issue is whether comparable requests are handled fairly under transparent applicable criteria.','republic-act-6713','informal-favoritism'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A report says the Constitution establishes a republican State. Which related principle is expressly stated in Article II, Section 1?','The Philippines is a democratic and republican State, and sovereignty resides in the people.',['Sovereignty resides in private corporations.','Government authority is unlimited.','Only courts possess sovereign authority.'],'Article II, Section 1 contains both the democratic/republican character and popular-sovereignty statement.','1987-philippine-constitution','republicanism-misread'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An office publishes meeting details only through an inaccessible channel. What should be considered?','Whether the notice method meaningfully enables affected people to participate.',['Whether publication occurred in any form, regardless of reach.','Whether affected people should find the notice themselves.','Whether accessibility is unrelated to participation.'],'A formal notice may not provide meaningful access if intended participants cannot use the channel.','1987-philippine-constitution','publication-equals-access'],
];
