 ['Compare the entry on the form with the ledger: Form “Bautista, Nilo, 04-118”; Ledger “Bautista, Nilo, 04-181.” What should be flagged?','The final three-digit code differs: 118 versus 181.',['The names differ.','The dates differ.','No mismatch is present.'],'The name matches; compare the code exactly and note the transposed digits.','record-cross-check','name-match-hides-id-error'],
 ['An envelope is labeled “District 08, Box 014” while the index says “District 08, Box 14.” What is the correct exact-match finding?','The box keys differ in leading-zero formatting.',['They are exact matches because the numeric value is equal.','The district differs.','The index has an extra district.'],'An exact record-key task preserves leading zeros when they appear in the stored identifier.','record-key-format','numeric-equivalence-normalizes-id'],
 ['A clerk must file these department names: “Budget Office,” “Budget Review,” “Building Services,” “Benefits Desk.” Which comes first?','Benefits Desk',['Budget Office','Budget Review','Building Services'],'Compare from the first letter; “Be” in Benefits precedes “Bu” in the other names.','filing-first-key','compare-later-letter'],
 ['An index uses numeric order: 3, 12, 21, 105. Which is the correct ascending sequence?','3, 12, 21, 105',['105, 12, 21, 3','12, 21, 3, 105','3, 21, 12, 105'],'Compare the values numerically rather than by character count.','numeric-filing-order','lexicographic-vs-numeric'],
 ['Which detail should be checked first when two paper records have the same name but different tracking numbers?','The tracking numbers, because they identify separate records.',['Assume one record is a duplicate.','Discard the record with more digits.','Change both numbers to match.'],'A shared name does not establish that two records are the same; compare the unique key.','record-identity','name-as-unique-key'],
 ['A filing rule says to alphabetize by organization, then by document title. Two records are “City Health Office—Annual Plan” and “City Health Office—Audit Report.” Which is first?','City Health Office—Annual Plan',['City Health Office—Audit Report','They tie and cannot be ordered.','The later-created file must come first.'],'The organization keys tie; compare titles next. “An” in Annual precedes “Au” in Audit.','multi-key-filing','ignore-secondary-key'],
 ['Two applications have the same applicant name but different reference numbers and receipt dates. What should the clerk do before classifying one as a duplicate?','Check the source records and apply the authorized duplicate criteria; the name alone is insufficient.',['Merge the applications because the names match.','Delete the later-dated application without review.','Change one reference number so the records match.'],'A name match does not establish record identity; compare unique identifiers and apply the documented duplicate rule.','duplicate-candidate-resolution','same-name-means-same-record'],
 ['A document is filed under “San Miguel, Ana” and the index reads “San Miguel, Anna.” What is the accurate comparison?','The given names differ by one repeated letter.',['The records match.','The surnames differ.','The middle initials differ.'],'The surnames match, but Ana and Anna are not identical strings.','name-field-comparison','near-match'],
 ['Which action best prevents a transposed-digit error during data entry?','Compare the entered identifier character by character with the source before saving.',['Rely on memory after one reading.','Remove all leading zeros first.','Sort the numbers and assume sequence.'],'A direct character-by-character check catches transpositions and preserves formatting.','verification-workflow','memory-as-check'],
