 ['cse-grammar-application','Which sentence uses “fewer” correctly?','Fewer applications were incomplete this week.',['Less applications were incomplete this week.','Fewer time was needed this week.','Fewest time was needed this week.'],'Fewer modifies countable plural applications.','count-modifier','less-fewer'],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The first estimate was based on a small sample; ___, the report avoids a broad conclusion.','therefore',['nevertheless','for example','in the same way'],'Therefore links the limitation to the cautious conclusion.','consequence-transition','contrast-for-consequence'],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','A passage states that the total increased but the rate declined. Which sentence best explains the relationship?','The number served rose, but the comparison base grew faster.',['The total and rate must move in the same direction.','A rate does not use a denominator.','The increase proves that every subgroup improved.'],'A faster-growing denominator can make a rate fall even when the numerator rises.','rate-explanation','count-rate-confusion'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A reviewer calls a table “incomplete for this question” because it omits the comparison period. What does incomplete mean here?','It lacks information needed for the specific comparison.',['Every value in it is false.','It has no usable information at all.','It is missing a page by definition.'],'The omission limits this comparison but does not make every table entry false.','contextual-vocabulary','limitation-as-falsity'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','The instruction says “unless a supervisor approves, do not release the file.” No approval is recorded. What action is supported?','Do not release the file on the stated facts.',['Release it because no one objected.','Assume approval was given.','Delete the file.'],'Unless introduces an exception that has not been shown to occur.','exception-clause','exception-assumed'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A notice says the schedule is “tentative pending confirmation.” Which interpretation is best?','The schedule may change because confirmation is still outstanding.',['The schedule is final.','The schedule is canceled.','Confirmation has no bearing on it.'],'Tentative and pending signal that the schedule is not yet confirmed.','status-qualification','tentative-as-final'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','A policy is “implemented gradually” across offices. Gradually means:','in stages over time.',['all at once.','without a plan.','only after completion.'],'Gradual implementation occurs progressively rather than simultaneously.','contextual-vocabulary','sequence-meaning'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','The analyst calls one explanation “plausible” but asks for corroboration. Plausible means:','reasonable or possible given the available facts.',['proven beyond any doubt.','impossible to test.','officially approved.'],'Plausibility is weaker than proof, which is why corroboration is still requested.','contextual-vocabulary','plausible-as-proven'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The district’s average completion time fell from 8 to 6 days. The report also says the number of incomplete submissions rose.” What should not be inferred?','That every applicant experienced a faster completion.',['That the reported average fell.','That incomplete submissions rose.','That both measures concern the district.'],'An average change does not show that every individual case improved.','reading-average-scope','average-as-every-case'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “A new notice increased the number of applications received. The report does not compare applications that met the requirements.” What is unknown?','Whether the number of complete or eligible applications increased.',['Whether receipts were counted.','Whether applications were received.','Whether the notice existed.'],'Total submissions do not establish how many were complete or eligible.','reading-outcome-definition','volume-as-quality'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “A branch’s total workload increased, while its staff count also increased.” Which comparison better describes workload per staff member?','Divide workload by staff count for each period.',['Compare only the totals.','Subtract the staff count from the workload without units.','Assume each employee handled the same number.'],'A per-person rate uses staff count as the denominator.','reading-rate-selection','total-as-per-capita'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The project met its target in two of three months, but missed the target in the third.” Which summary is accurate?','It met the target in most reported months, but not all.',['It met the target every month.','It never met the target.','The monthly results cannot be summarized.'],'Two of three is most, but the third month prevents an all-month claim.','reading-quantifier','most-as-all'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The report identifies an association between training attendance and fewer errors, but employees self-selected whether to attend.” What limitation follows?','Attendees may differ from nonattendees in ways that affect errors.',['Training cannot affect errors.','The association proves causation.','Self-selection guarantees equal groups.'],'Self-selection can produce group differences beyond training itself.','reading-selection-bias','association-as-causation'],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','A recommendation is based on one observed error and a proposed control. Which addition would best strengthen it?','Evidence that the control addresses the error mechanism and can be monitored.',['A claim that all errors have one cause.','An unrelated office history.','A guarantee with no follow-up measure.'],'A recommendation is stronger when mechanism and monitoring are specified.','recommendation-support','solution-without-mechanism'],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Select the sentence with correct punctuation after an introductory dependent clause.','Because the source file was unavailable, the reviewer marked the result provisional.',['Because the source file was unavailable the reviewer, marked the result provisional.','Because, the source file was unavailable the reviewer marked the result provisional.','Because the source file was unavailable; the reviewer marked the result provisional.'],'A comma follows the introductory dependent clause.','introductory-clause-punctuation','comma-after-subject'],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which version avoids a misplaced “only” when the intent is that one employee—not the entire team—checked the log?','Only Mara checked the log.',['Mara checked only the log.','Mara only checked the log, not the other records.','Mara checked the log only after the review.'],'Only before Mara limits who performed the action.','limiting-modifier','modifier-scope'],
 ['cse-pronoun-reference','Which revision makes clear that the original form—not the copy—was signed?','The original form was signed; the copy was left unsigned.',['It was signed after it was copied.','The form and copy signed it.','The copy signed the original after that.'],'The revision names each document and its status, avoiding ambiguous it references.','pronoun-reference','ambiguous-document-reference'],
 ['cse-parallel-structure','Which sentence presents parallel reasons for a delay?','The delay resulted from a missing approval, an incomplete attachment, and a system outage.',['The delay resulted from a missing approval, an attachment that was incomplete, and the system went out.','The delay resulted because approval was missing, an incomplete attachment, and system outage.','The delay resulted from missing approval, attachment incomplete, and when the system failed.'],'The list uses parallel noun phrases for all three reasons.','parallel-noun-list','mixed-list-structure'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A passage says a decision is “without prejudice to later verification.” What does that qualification indicate?','Later verification may still affect the matter.',['The decision cannot ever be reviewed.','Verification has already confirmed every fact.','The decision is unrelated to the facts.'],'The phrase preserves the possibility of subsequent checking or adjustment.','legal-qualification-reading','qualification-ignored'],
];
foreach($verbalTail as $r)$add(['concept'=>$r[0],'stem'=>$r[1],'answer'=>$r[2],'wrong'=>$r[3],'why'=>$r[4],'family'=>$r[5],'misconception'=>$r[6],'depth'=>in_array($r[0],['cse-reading-comprehension','cse-paragraph-organization'],true)?4:3,'version'=>$r[0]==='cse-contextual-inference'&&str_contains($r[1],'prejudice')]);

/* Additional source-grounded language items emphasize inference and editing, not word-list variants. */
$verbalExtension=[
 ['cse-grammar-application','Choose the sentence that keeps the subject and verb in agreement.','The list of verified applicants is attached.',['The list of verified applicants are attached.','The list of verified applicants were attach.','The list of verified applicants have attached.'],'The head subject is the singular noun list; the prepositional phrase does not change its number.','agreement-head-subject','nearest-noun-agreement'],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which revision removes the dangling modifier?','After reviewing the totals, Mara corrected the report.',['After reviewing the totals, the report was corrected by Mara.','After reviewing the totals, a correction was necessary.','The totals, after reviewing, Mara corrected the report.'],'The introductory phrase now modifies the person who performed the review.','modifier-attachment','modifier-with-no-agent'],
 ['cse-parallel-structure','Which sentence presents the three review tasks in parallel form?','The team checked dates, verified signatures, and compared totals.',['The team checked dates, signatures were verified, and comparing totals.','The team checked dates, to verify signatures, and totals were compared.','The team was checking dates, verification of signatures, and compared totals.'],'The list uses three coordinated past-tense verbs with the same grammatical form.','parallel-verb-list','mixed-grammatical-form'],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The source record was unavailable; ___, the result was marked provisional.','therefore',['however','for instance','similarly'],'The second clause is a consequence of the unavailable source record.','consequence-transition','contrast-for-consequence'],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Choose the correctly punctuated sentence.','The clerk checked the date, the signature, and the attached receipt.',['The clerk checked the date the signature and, the attached receipt.','The clerk checked, the date, the signature and the attached receipt.','The clerk checked the date; the signature; and, the attached receipt.'],'Commas consistently separate the three parallel items in the series.','list-punctuation','inconsistent-list-separators'],
 ['cse-pronoun-reference','Which sentence makes clear that the approval—not the request—was delayed?','The request was complete, but its approval was delayed.',['It was complete, but it was delayed.','The request was complete, but it delayed approval.','The approval was complete, but it requested a delay.'],'Naming approval directly prevents the pronoun from having an unclear referent.','pronoun-reference-clarity','ambiguous-it'],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','A paragraph explains that a count rose, identifies the denominator, then cautions against causal claims. Which order is clearest?','Observed count → denominator/context → limitation on interpretation.',['Causal conclusion → unrelated detail → observed count.','Limitation → unsupported cause → denominator omitted.','Recommendation → new topic → count with no context.'],'The reader first sees what changed, then how to interpret its base, and finally what the evidence cannot establish.','data-explanation-order','conclusion-before-evidence'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A memo describes a figure as “preliminary pending reconciliation.” What is the best reading?','The figure may change after the records are compared and differences resolved.',['The figure is knowingly false.','Reconciliation has already confirmed it.','The figure cannot be used even provisionally.'],'Pending reconciliation indicates that the comparison step is outstanding; it does not establish falsity.','preliminary-context','pending-as-false'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','The reviewer calls the claim “qualified” because it applies only to complete files. Qualified most nearly means:','limited by a stated condition.',['proved without limitation.','unrelated to the files.','withdrawn as false.'],'The complete-file condition narrows the claim’s scope.','qualified-claim','qualification-as-proof'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The office reduced the form from four pages to two. It did not measure completion errors after the change.” Which conclusion is supported?','The form became shorter; the effect on completion errors is unknown.',['Errors necessarily declined.','Errors necessarily increased.','Every user completed the shorter form.'],'The passage reports length but provides no error outcome.','reading-unmeasured-outcome','design-change-as-outcome'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The monthly average fell from 12 days to 9 days. The report does not show individual case times.” What cannot be concluded?','That every individual case was completed three days faster.',['That the reported average fell.','That the two averages differ by three days.','That individual times were not shown.'],'A group average does not describe the change for each individual case.','reading-average-and-individuals','average-as-every-case'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “A branch received 80 complete applications and approved 60. The report excludes incomplete submissions.” What does the approval rate directly describe?','Approvals among the 80 complete applications included in the report.',['All people who considered applying.','Every submission, including incomplete ones.','All residents served by the branch.'],'The stated base is the 80 complete applications; broader populations are not measured.','reading-denominator-boundary','denominator-expansion'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “A reminder was introduced in May. Missed visits fell, while the office also added appointment slots.” What is the strongest conclusion?','Missed visits fell after both changes, but the reminder’s separate effect is uncertain.',['The reminder alone caused the decline.','Added slots had no effect.','The reported decline is impossible.'],'The two concurrent changes prevent identifying the isolated effect from the information given.','reading-multiple-interventions','single-cause-attribution'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A notice says a request is “eligible for review” after initial screening. What follows?','The request may proceed to review; approval is not yet established.',['The request has been approved.','The request must be denied.','The review has already finished.'],'Eligibility to enter a process is not the outcome of that process.','process-stage-inference','stage-as-outcome'],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','A report states that total submissions rose while the completion rate fell. Which sentence best explains how both can be true?','The number of completed submissions may have risen more slowly than the total number received.',['A completion rate does not use a denominator.','A larger total guarantees a larger completion rate.','The report must contain a contradiction.'],'A rate depends on both the numerator and denominator, so the total can rise while the proportion declines.','count-rate-cohesion','count-rate-confusion'],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The two totals use different definitions; ___, they should not be compared until the definitions are aligned.','accordingly',['nevertheless','for example','meanwhile'],'Accordingly introduces the action that follows from the stated difference.','logical-connector','contrast-for-consequence'],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Which sentence uses a clear comparison?','The revised process took fewer days than the previous process.',['The revised process took fewer days than before it.','The revised process was faster than the previous process took days.','The revised process took less days than the previous process.'],'The comparison places like measures—days required by each process—side by side.','comparison-parallelism','unmatched-comparison'],
 ['cse-grammar-application','Choose the clearest sentence for a report about two possible causes.','The delay may reflect either the missing record or the later review date.',['The delay may reflect either the missing record or because review was later.','Either the delay may reflect the missing record or the review was later.','The delay may reflect either the missing record or reviewing later by them.'],'Either introduces two grammatically parallel alternatives.','correlative-conjunction-parallelism','either-or-mismatch'],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Passage: “The survey received 40 responses from 300 invited users. Most respondents preferred the new schedule.” What limitation matters most?','The respondents may not represent all invited users.',['The 40 responses prove no one liked the old schedule.','The result includes every invited user.','The survey establishes why each person preferred the schedule.'],'A low response fraction can limit generalization even if the reported respondents are described accurately.','reading-nonresponse','respondents-as-population'],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A reviewer says the data “support but do not settle” the proposal. What does this mean?','The data favor the proposal but leave relevant uncertainty.',['The data conclusively prove the proposal.','The data contradict the proposal.','No evidence was considered.'],'Support is not the same as conclusive proof, and the phrase expressly preserves uncertainty.','evidence-qualification','support-as-certainty'],
 ['cse-word-meaning','In a report, “The totals are consistent across the two ledgers” most nearly means the totals:','agree with one another.',['are written in the same handwriting.','are guaranteed accurate.','were produced at the same time.'],'The comparison concerns agreement between the recorded totals, not a guarantee about their accuracy.','contextual-word-meaning','agreement-as-accuracy'],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','A short response must state a recommendation, explain its evidence, and note a limitation. Which order is most transparent?','Recommendation → supporting evidence → limitation.',['Limitation → unrelated fact → recommendation without support.','Evidence → a different recommendation → no limitation.','Conclusion → claim of certainty → evidence omitted.'],'The structure makes the recommendation and its basis visible while bounding what the evidence shows.','recommendation-structure','unsupported-recommendation'],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Basahin: “Hindi pa pinal ang bilang; isinasama pa ang mga tala mula sa huling tanggapan.” Ano ang pinakamainam na kahulugan ng “hindi pa pinal” sa konteksto?','Maaari pang magbago matapos maisama at mapatunayan ang mga tala.',['Tiyak na mali ang bilang.','Hindi na maaaring gamitin ang anumang tala.','Napatunayan nang hindi na magbabago ang bilang.'],'Ipinakikita ng pangungusap na may mga tala pang idaragdag, kaya hindi pa pinal ang bilang.','filipino-context-inference','preliminary-as-false'],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Basahin: “Bumaba ang kabuuang reklamo, ngunit tumaas ang bahagdan dahil mas kaunti ang transaksiyong pinaghambingan.” Aling paliwanag ang wasto?','Maaaring bumaba ang bilang ngunit tumaas ang rate kapag mas mabilis lumiit ang denominator.',['Laging magkapareho ang direksiyon ng bilang at rate.','Hindi gumagamit ng denominator ang bahagdan.','Pinatutunayan ng pagbabago na mali ang tala.'],'Magkaiba ang kabuuang bilang at rate; nakaaapekto sa rate ang bilang ng mga transaksiyon.','filipino-rate-inference','count-rate-confusion'],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Basahin: “May kaugnayan ang paalala sa pagbaba ng pagliban, ngunit kasabay nito ang pagbabago ng oras ng serbisyo.” Ano ang maingat na hinuha?','Nakita ang pagbaba, ngunit hindi matitiyak ang hiwalay na epekto ng paalala.',['Paalala lamang ang sanhi ng pagbaba.','Walang naganap na pagbaba.','Walang epekto ang pagbabago ng oras.'],'May dalawang pagbabagong naganap kaya hindi maihihiwalay ang sanhi batay lamang sa pahayag.','filipino-causal-inference','association-as-cause'],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Sa ulat, “bahagya lamang ang pagtaas at hindi ito sapat upang patunayang tuloy-tuloy ang trend.” Ano ang ipinahihiwatig?','May naitalang pagtaas, ngunit kulang ang batayan para sa pangmatagalang konklusyon.',['Patuloy na tataas ang bilang.','Walang anumang pagbabago.','Tiyak na mali ang ulat.'],'Nililimitahan ng pahayag ang konklusyon sa naobserbahang pagtaas.','filipino-qualified-conclusion','single-change-as-trend'],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Basahin: “Isinama sa talaan ang mga nakumpletong kahilingan lamang; hindi kasama ang mga hindi nakarating sa huling hakbang.” Aling grupo ang maaaring hindi makita sa bilang?','Mga taong nakaranas ng hadlang bago makumpleto ang proseso.',['Lahat ng nakumpleto ang proseso.','Mga kahilingang naitala sa huling hakbang.','Mga opisyal na gumawa ng talaan.'],'Ang bilang ay nagsisimula lamang sa mga nakumpleto, kaya maaaring hindi makita ang mga nahadlangan nang mas maaga.','filipino-denominator-scope','completion-only-population'],
];
