/* General Information extension: primary-source civic reasoning, with every item receiving a live-source check. */
$giExtension=[
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A public office reports how it corrected an inaccurate total and keeps the original computation for audit. Which constitutional principle is most directly reflected?','Public office is a public trust, with accountability to the people.',['Public records belong personally to the employee.','An error should be concealed once corrected.','Accountability applies only after an election.'],'Article XI, Section 1 describes public office as a public trust and public officers/employees as accountable to the people.','1987-philippine-constitution','correction-with-audit-trail'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A resident asks which constitutional principle locates ultimate sovereignty in the people. Which statement answers directly?','Sovereignty resides in the people and all government authority emanates from them.',['Authority originates solely in appointed offices.','Sovereignty is divided among private organizations.','Government authority is independent of the people.'],'Article II, Section 1 states that sovereignty resides in the people and government authority emanates from them.','1987-philippine-constitution','popular-sovereignty'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','An agency reviews a rule that may burden one group differently. Which constitutional safeguard is directly relevant to a person claiming unequal legal treatment?','Equal protection of the laws, applied to the facts and governing rules.',['A guarantee that every policy produces identical outcomes.','A rule that all distinctions are automatically unlawful.','A requirement that public services have no eligibility criteria.'],'Article III, Section 1 includes equal protection; whether a distinction is lawful requires the relevant facts and doctrine.','1987-philippine-constitution','equal-protection-as-identical-outcome'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A group forms a lawful association for a purpose not contrary to law. Which constitutional protection is most directly relevant?','The right of the people to form unions, associations, or societies for purposes not contrary to law.',['A right to compel the government to adopt every group proposal.','A guarantee that private associations may enter any property.','A right to disregard generally applicable lawful rules.'],'Article III, Section 8 protects the right to form associations for purposes not contrary to law.','1987-philippine-constitution','association-as-policy-control',4,true],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','Government acquires private land for a public road. Which constitutional condition applies to the taking?','Private property may not be taken for public use without just compensation.',['A public purpose eliminates compensation.','Compensation is due only if the owner approves the project.','Any public announcement automatically completes the taking.'],'Article III, Section 9 bars taking private property for public use without just compensation.','1987-philippine-constitution','eminent-domain-without-compensation',4,true],
 ['cse-government-functions','A public office executes a valid statute through administrative action but may not create an exception contrary to that statute. Which principle controls?','Administrative implementation must remain within the Constitution and law.',['An agency may disregard a statute whenever implementation is difficult.','Implementation transfers legislative power to each employee.','A written procedure outranks the statute it implements.'],'Executive and administrative implementation operates under governing law rather than replacing it.','1987-philippine-constitution','implementation-as-independent-law'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','Investigators question a person in custodial investigation. Which safeguard does Article III, Section 12 specifically address?','The right to be informed of the right to remain silent and to have competent, independent counsel.',['A right to select the investigating agency.','A guarantee that no investigation may occur.','A right to automatic dismissal.'],'Section 12 states custodial-investigation safeguards, including notice of the right to silence and counsel.','1987-philippine-constitution','custodial-safeguard-overclaim'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person asks whether a search of a home may occur without a warrant. The scenario gives no facts about a recognized exception. What is the safest constitutional answer?','The protection against unreasonable searches is implicated; no exception is established by the stated facts.',['Every warrantless search is valid.','Every search is valid if an officer requests it.','The Constitution gives no protection to homes.'],'Article III, Section 2 protects persons and houses against unreasonable searches and seizures; the item supplies no exception facts.','1987-philippine-constitution','exception-without-facts'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A case remains unresolved for an undue period despite the parties being ready to proceed. Which constitutional protection may be relevant?','The right to speedy disposition of cases.',['A right to a predetermined outcome.','A rule that every delay requires dismissal.','A right to select the deciding tribunal.'],'Article III, Section 16 recognizes the right to speedy disposition of cases before judicial, quasi-judicial, or administrative bodies; the remedy depends on the circumstances.','1987-philippine-constitution','delay-as-automatic-dismissal'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A citizen requests information on a matter of public concern. What is the most accurate constitutional framing?','There is a right to information on matters of public concern, subject to limitations provided by law.',['Every confidential record must be released without screening.','No government information may be requested.','The requester may alter the record after access.'],'Article III, Section 7 recognizes the right while expressly allowing limitations provided by law.','1987-philippine-constitution','access-as-unlimited'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A report alleges degrading treatment, but the facts have not been independently established. What response best respects dignity and fair process?','Protect those at risk, preserve evidence, and investigate through appropriate procedures without presenting an allegation as a finding.',['Publish unverified identifying details immediately.','Dismiss the concern until every fact is final.','Announce guilt before investigation.'],'Human dignity calls for serious attention; reliable fact-finding distinguishes allegations from established findings.','universal-declaration-human-rights','allegation-as-finding'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A public-service form is available only in a format some intended users cannot access. What should the agency examine?','Whether an accessible alternative is needed to provide meaningful access under applicable rules.',['Whether identical format alone proves equal access.','Whether affected users should be excluded from statistics.','Whether all alternative formats are prohibited.'],'Formal sameness may leave an access barrier; applicable rights and duties should be evaluated against the facts.','1987-philippine-constitution','formal-equality-as-access'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A statement compares two groups but gives no information about how people were selected. What should a reader avoid concluding?','That the observed difference necessarily reflects an inherent difference between the groups.',['That selection details could matter.','That the report contains two groups.','That additional context may improve interpretation.'],'Selection and measurement can explain observed differences; the stated comparison alone cannot establish an inherent cause.','universal-declaration-human-rights','group-difference-as-inherent'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A consultation receives comments from residents, and staff must still assess them under the governing criteria. Which conclusion is sound?','Comments inform consideration but do not by themselves dictate the final decision.',['Every comment must be adopted.','Participation removes the need to follow law.','A decision is invalid unless every commenter agrees.'],'Participation supplies views and information; applicable criteria still govern the decision.','1987-philippine-constitution','participation-as-veto'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An online consultation excludes residents without reliable internet. What improvement most directly addresses the identified access gap?','Provide an accessible alternative channel and document how submissions are considered.',['Treat nonresponse as consent.','Assume all residents have reliable internet.','Close the consultation early.'],'An alternative channel makes participation more accessible to the identified group; documenting review makes the process transparent.','1987-philippine-constitution','nonresponse-as-consent'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A community group disagrees with a proposal but has not supplied evidence about its likely effects. What is the most responsible agency response?','Record the view, identify relevant evidence, and apply the published decision criteria.',['Treat disagreement as proof of harm.','Ignore all views that oppose the proposal.','Change the criteria for each commenter.'],'Participation is meaningful when views are fairly considered alongside evidence and consistently applied criteria.','1987-philippine-constitution','view-as-proof'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A published performance rate excluded a category of completed cases. What is the most accountable action?','Correct or qualify the reported measure and retain a traceable explanation of the revision.',['Leave it unchanged to avoid scrutiny.','Delete the source data.','Replace it with an undocumented estimate.'],'Transparent correction preserves the record and makes the measure’s scope understandable.','republic-act-6713','silent-correction'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','Two reports disagree because one includes pending cases. Before announcing which office performed better, what should be done?','Align the inclusion definitions and compare the measures on a common basis.',['Select the larger figure as automatically more accurate.','Average the incompatible totals.','Ignore the difference in definitions.'],'The reports do not measure the same population until pending cases are treated consistently.','republic-act-6713','unlike-denominators'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A supervisor asks an employee to destroy an original calculation after a correction. What is the defensible response?','Preserve the original and follow authorized correction and records procedures.',['Destroy it so only the corrected value remains.','Backdate the revised report.','Send the data to a personal account.'],'A traceable correction supports accountability and follows applicable records procedures.','republic-act-6713','audit-trail-destruction'],
 ['cse-public-interest','Two requests are otherwise alike, but the applicants support different political parties. How should a public employee handle them?','Apply the same lawful service criteria without unfair discrimination based on party affiliation or preference.',['Prioritize the applicant who supports the employee’s party.','Delay the request from the opposing party without review.','Change the criteria according to political preference.'],'RA 6713 names political neutrality and directs public officials and employees to provide service without unfair discrimination regardless of party affiliation or preference.','ra6713-political-neutrality','partisan-service'],
 ['cse-conflict-of-interest','An employee of an agency that regulates a private company is offered a paid officer role in that company while still employed by the agency. Under RA 6713 Section 7(b)(1), which statement is most accurate?','During incumbency, holding an officer or employee role in a private enterprise regulated by the employee’s office is prohibited unless expressly allowed by law.',['It is always permitted if the employee does not personally inspect the company.','It is permitted whenever the employee donates the salary.','It is prohibited only after the employee has approved a transaction.'],'Section 7(b)(1) restricts specified employment or positions in a private enterprise regulated, supervised, or licensed by the employee’s office unless expressly allowed by law.','ra6713-regulated-private-enterprise','no-personal-inspection-as-exception'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','Two similar requests come from citizens with different political affiliations. Which approach reflects political neutrality?','Apply the same lawful criteria to both requests.',['Prioritize the political supporter.','Refuse the request from the opposing group without review.','Change the criteria based on affiliation.'],'RA 6713 lists political neutrality among norms of conduct; service decisions should not rest on partisan preference.','republic-act-6713','partisan-service'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee uses a government vehicle for a private errand without authorization. Which concern is most direct?','Use of public resources must follow applicable official-purpose rules.',['Any private use is automatically permitted if brief.','Public resources belong to the employee during free time.','The trip should be removed from records.'],'Public resources are entrusted for official functions; applicable rules govern any permitted use.','republic-act-6713','public-resource-private-use'],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A citizen writes an official communication concerning a matter within an office’s authority. What response-time rule does RA 6713 generally state for written communications?','Respond within 15 working days from receipt, subject to the law’s terms.',['Respond within 15 calendar months.','Respond only if the citizen visits in person.','No response is required for written communications.'],'RA 6713 Section 5(a) directs responses within 15 working days from receipt, subject to its terms.','republic-act-6713','working-days-confusion'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','During development of a city or municipal solid-waste plan, what process does RA 9003 direct the local board to conduct?','Consultation with the various sectors of the community.',['Consultation only after implementation is complete.','Consultation limited to private haulers.','No consultation because the plan is purely technical.'],'RA 9003 directs the local board to consult community sectors during plan development.','ra9003-plan-consultation','consultation-after-finalization'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Under RA 9003, where should a materials recovery facility be established?','In every barangay or cluster of barangays.',['Only at the national level.','Only beside a sanitary landfill in each province.','Only in cities with more than one million residents.'],'Section 32 provides for an MRF in every barangay or cluster of barangays; this does not make it a substitute for source segregation.','ra9003-mrf-location','national-only-facility'],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A report shows less waste collected after a segregation campaign, but it does not measure illegal dumping. What limitation should be stated?','The collection figure alone does not establish that total waste generation or improper disposal fell.',['All waste must have disappeared.','The campaign necessarily failed.','Collection totals measure every disposal pathway.'],'A collection measure does not capture unobserved pathways such as dumping or changes in generation.','republic-act-9003','measured-channel-as-total'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A facility’s emissions may affect nearby residents. Which law principally addresses air-pollution prevention and control?','Republic Act No. 8749, the Philippine Clean Air Act of 1999.',['RA 9003, the solid-waste management law.','RA 6713, the public-service ethics law.','The UDHR alone.'],'RA 8749 is the Philippine Clean Air Act of 1999, concerned with air-quality management and pollution prevention/control.','republic-act-8749','air-vs-solid-waste-law'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','Smoke readings fall after a local intervention, but weather and industrial activity also change. Which conclusion is most defensible?','The readings fell; the intervention’s isolated causal effect is not established.',['The intervention caused the entire change.','Weather and activity cannot affect readings.','The observation must be discarded.'],'Concurrent factors are plausible alternative explanations even while the measured trend remains reportable.','republic-act-8749','trend-as-cause'],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A proposed detention practice relies on degrading treatment to obtain cooperation. Which constitutional safeguard is most directly relevant?','Protection against torture, force, violence, threats, or other means that vitiate free will.',['A rule that any accusation proves guilt.','A guarantee that no lawful questioning may occur.','A right to choose the investigating agency.'],'Article III, Section 12(2) prohibits torture and other coercive means that vitiate free will.','1987-philippine-constitution','coercion-as-permitted-investigation'],
 ['cse-public-interest','A service notice names a deadline but not who must act or where to submit the document. Which revision best serves the public?','State the affected group, required action, deadline, and submission channel accurately.',['Add technical terms without defining the action.','Remove contact details.','Assume every reader knows the process.'],'Clear, accurate instructions support responsive public service and reduce preventable access errors.','republic-act-6713','technicality-as-clarity'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A policy review concerns a project that may affect environmental health. Which constitutional state policy is directly relevant?','The State shall protect and advance the people’s right to a balanced and healthful ecology.',['The Constitution excludes environmental concerns.','Environmental protection is exclusively private.','Natural resources cannot be part of public policy.'],'Article II, Section 16 states the policy concerning a balanced and healthful ecology.','1987-philippine-constitution','ecology-policy-omission'],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A resident asks which institution audits government accounts and expenditures. Which constitutional Commission is responsible?','The Commission on Audit.',['The Commission on Elections.','The Civil Service Commission.','The Commission on Human Rights.'],'Article IX-D establishes the Commission on Audit and its audit functions.','1987-philippine-constitution','constitutional-commission-confusion'],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A government rule targets a person solely for peaceful religious practice. Which constitutional freedom is most directly implicated?','Freedom of religion, including the free exercise of religious profession and worship, subject to constitutional limits.',['A guarantee that every religious claim overrides all neutral laws.','A right to enter any private property.','A guarantee of a particular public benefit.'],'Article III, Section 5 protects free exercise and enjoyment of religious profession and worship, subject to constitutional limits.','1987-philippine-constitution','free-exercise-as-unlimited-exemption'],
 ['cse-government-functions','Congress creates a general rule through legislation, while an agency applies it to individual filings. Which distinction is accurate?','Congress exercises legislative power; the agency administers the law within its authority.',['The agency’s individual filing decisions are all legislation.','Courts enact the statute by resolving a filing.','A filing replaces the enacted rule.'],'Article VI assigns legislative power to Congress; administrative bodies implement governing law within delegated authority.','1987-philippine-constitution','administration-as-legislation'],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A report uses an average but omits that one branch served twice as many people. What should be added for a fairer comparison?','A relevant denominator or rate, with definitions and periods made comparable.',['A claim that the larger average proves poorer service.','The branch names only.','A second average with no base.'],'A population-adjusted measure helps compare offices with different service volumes, while definitions and time periods remain important.','republic-act-6713','raw-average-as-fair-comparison'],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An agency receives public comments but does not adopt one proposal. Which fact would best show that participation was still meaningful?','The agency documented the comments, evaluated them against stated criteria, and explained its decision.',['Every comment was adopted.','The final policy was unchanged, so no review occurred.','The agency counted comments but discarded them without consideration.'],'Meaningful consideration can be evidenced by transparent review; participation does not imply a veto.','1987-philippine-constitution','outcome-as-only-proof-of-participation'],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A city reports fewer collected plastic items after a cleanup event. Which follow-up measure would better test broader waste-management progress?','Track waste generation and disposal pathways over a defined period, alongside collection data.',['Count only items in the cleanup area once.','Assume collected items represent all waste.','Stop measuring after the event.'],'A single cleanup count is narrow; broader indicators and a time frame help assess generation and management.','republic-act-9003','one-event-as-system-outcome'],
];
