 ['cse-reading-comprehension','A passage says a branch introduced a queue ticket, but does not report waiting times before the change. What does the passage not establish?','That the ticket reduced waiting time.',['That the branch introduced a ticket.','That tickets were issued.','That a queue existed.'],'A reduction requires a comparable measure before and after or another suitable comparison.','reading-before-after-evidence','intervention-as-effect',4],
 ['cse-contextual-inference','A reviewer says an explanation is “plausible but unverified.” What should the reader do with it?','Treat it as a possible explanation, not an established fact.',['Treat it as proven because it is plausible.','Reject it as impossible.','Ignore any later verification.'],'Plausibility allows consideration; lack of verification prevents treating it as established.','status-of-explanation','plausibility-as-proof',3],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','A notice directs readers to submit “the signed original, not a photocopy.” Which item satisfies the instruction?','The signed original document.',['An unsigned original.','A signed photocopy.','An unsigned photocopy.'],'Both stated attributes—signed and original—are required.','reading-multiple-constraints','one-condition-satisfies',2],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','A sentence begins “By contrast,” but the preceding sentence describes a similar result. What revision best fixes the transition?','Replace “By contrast” with a transition that signals addition or similarity.',['Keep it because transitions are interchangeable.','Delete the preceding evidence.','Add a second contrast marker.'],'The transition should express the actual relation between adjacent ideas.','transition-relation','transition-as-decoration',3],
