 ['cse-paragraph-organization','A paragraph makes a broad claim, gives two records supporting it, then notes that the records came from one office. What should its conclusion do?','State the claim cautiously and limit it to the evidence from that office.',['Generalize it to every office.','Ignore the records and repeat the claim.','Treat one-office evidence as proof of national effect.'],'The scope of the conclusion must reflect the source’s limited setting.','bounded-conclusion','local-to-universal',4],
