 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is jailed solely for failing to repay a private loan, with no separate criminal offense stated. Which constitutional provision is directly relevant?','The Constitution prohibits imprisonment for debt.',['A guarantee of a particular public job.','A right to avoid every civil proceeding.','A rule that every unpaid claim is automatically canceled.'],'Article III, Section 20 states that no person shall be imprisoned for debt; the scenario identifies no separate offense.','1987-philippine-constitution','debt-as-criminal-imprisonment',3],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A person is deprived of liberty without notice or a fair opportunity to respond. Which general constitutional safeguard is implicated?','Due process of law.',['The right to vote in every agency decision.','The rule that every allegation is true.','An automatic right to a particular outcome.'],'Article III, Section 1 protects life, liberty, and property through due process.','gi-due-process','process-as-guaranteed-outcome',3],
 ['cse-bill-of-rights','A citizen asks for government information about a matter of public concern. Which statement best describes the constitutional principle?','The right of access is recognized, subject to limitations provided by law.',['Every government record must always be disclosed.','No public information may be requested.','Access depends only on personal agreement of an employee.'],'Article III, Section 7 recognizes access to official records on matters of public concern, subject to legal limitations.','gi-access-to-information','right-as-unlimited',4],
 ['cse-government-functions','Congress enacts a statute and an agency applies it to permit applications. Which distinction is accurate?','Congress exercises legislative power; the agency administers the law within its authority.',['The agency’s individual decisions are statutes.','The courts enact the statute by reviewing a case.','A permit replaces the governing law.'],'The Constitution assigns legislative power to Congress; administration applies enacted law within authorized bounds.','gi-legislative-administrative-role','administration-as-legislation',3],
 ['cse-government-functions','A court resolves a dispute over how a statute applies to a case. Which government function is being exercised?','Judicial power.',['Legislative power.','The audit function.','The election function.'],'Article VIII vests judicial power in the Supreme Court and lower courts established by law.','gi-judicial-function','court-as-lawmaker',2],
 ['cse-government-functions','Which constitutional commission audits government accounts and expenditures?','The Commission on Audit.',['The Commission on Elections.','The Civil Service Commission.','The Commission on Human Rights.'],'Article IX-D establishes the Commission on Audit and its audit responsibilities.','gi-constitutional-commissions','commission-function-confusion',2],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A policy review concerns an activity that may affect environmental health. Which constitutional state policy is directly relevant?','The State shall protect and advance the people’s right to a balanced and healthful ecology.',['Environmental protection is exclusively private.','The Constitution excludes ecological concerns.','Natural resources cannot be part of public policy.'],'Article II, Section 16 states the policy concerning a balanced and healthful ecology.','gi-ecology-policy','policy-omission',3],
 ['cse-constitutional-principles','A public office handles a matter affecting residents from different communities. Which constitutional principle supports equal treatment under applicable law?','Equal protection of the laws.',['Preferential treatment based only on personal connections.','Different rules for similarly situated people without a lawful basis.','Public convenience always overrides legal rights.'],'Article III, Section 1 includes equal protection of the laws.','gi-equal-protection','connection-as-entitlement',3],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A rule is written formally, but its application treats similarly situated people differently without a lawful basis. What should the reviewer examine?','Whether the distinction has a legitimate legal basis and is applied consistently with equal protection.',['Whether the rule is written, which alone proves fairness.','Whether the affected people agree with the result.','Whether the distinction is convenient for the office.'],'Formal publication alone does not resolve whether a classification is lawful; equal-protection principles matter.','gi-formal-rule-review','written-rule-as-fairness',4],
 ['cse-public-accountability','A report identifies a possible error in public accounts. Which response best reflects accountability?','Preserve the records, document the issue, and refer it through the authorized review process.',['Alter the source figures to match the summary.','Delete the report before review.','Assign blame before checking the records.'],'Public office is a public trust; a documented, reviewable process supports accountability.','gi-accountability-records','concealment-as-resolution',4],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An agency receives public comments but does not adopt one proposal. What fact would best show that participation was still considered?','The agency documented and evaluated the comments against stated criteria before explaining its decision.',['Every comment was adopted.','The final policy was unchanged, so no review occurred.','Opposing comments were discarded without consideration.'],'Participation supports consideration; it does not itself dictate the outcome.','gi-participation-evidence','outcome-as-only-proof',4],
 ['cse-public-interest','An official responds within the period required by RA 6713, but the reply only says “received.” What must the reply also state under Section 5(a)?','The action taken on the request.',['The employee’s party affiliation.','A guarantee that the requested outcome will be granted.','The applicant’s unrelated personal information.'],'Section 5(a) requires a reply to state the action taken; timely acknowledgment alone does not fulfill that content requirement.','ra6713-response-content','acknowledgment-as-action',4],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public employee is asked to favor a relative’s application over other complete applications. What response best reflects ethical public service?','Apply the same lawful criteria and disclose or manage any relevant conflict under applicable rules.',['Move the relative to the front of the queue.','Hide the relationship because the application is complete.','Change the criteria only for that applicant.'],'RA 6713 emphasizes public interest, justness, sincerity, and professionalism; relevant conflicts should not distort official action.','gi-fair-service','relationship-as-priority',4],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A citizen asks about a step the employee has not verified. What is the most responsible response?','Provide verified information and check the uncertain detail before stating it as fact.',['Guess to avoid delay.','Invent a standard answer.','Refuse all assistance even if other information is verified.'],'RA 6713 norms include responsiveness and professionalism; accuracy requires communicating what is verified.','gi-verified-response','speed-over-accuracy',3],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A public employee uses office time and resources for an unrelated private business task. Which principle is most directly implicated?','Commitment to public interest and proper use of public resources.',['Political neutrality requires the employee to endorse a candidate.','Public resources may be used for any private purpose.','The task is automatically authorized if brief.'],'RA 6713’s norms of conduct orient public service toward public interest; specific workplace rules may add controls.','gi-public-resources','private-use-as-harmless',3],
 ['cse-conflict-of-interest','A licensed professional in public service wants to accept a private-practice engagement. Under RA 6713 Section 7(b)(2), which condition applies?','The practice must be authorized by the Constitution or law and must not conflict or tend to conflict with official functions.',['It is permitted whenever the client is not a government office.','It is permitted if the employee completes public duties after hours, regardless of conflict.','It is always prohibited for every public employee, even when law authorizes it.'],'Section 7(b)(2) permits private practice only when authorized by the Constitution or law and when it does not conflict or tend to conflict with official functions.','ra6713-private-practice-limit','after-hours-as-no-conflict',4],
 ['cse-public-interest','A service unit changes its published eligibility criteria during review of one favored applicant. What is the central concern?','Unequal and potentially arbitrary application of the criteria.',['The criteria must always remain unchanged even when law requires revision.','The applicant’s name is too short.','A published rule cannot affect public service.'],'Consistent, just administration requires applying lawful criteria fairly rather than tailoring them for favoritism.','gi-consistent-criteria','favoritism-as-flexibility',4],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A supervisor asks staff to promote a candidate using government communication channels. Which RA 6713 norm is most directly relevant?','Political neutrality in public service.',['Simple living.','Environmental stewardship.','The audit of private household expenses.'],'RA 6713 lists political neutrality among the norms of conduct for public officials and employees.','gi-political-neutrality','official-channel-as-campaign-tool',3],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','An employee receives a complaint about a delayed service. Which response best aligns with responsiveness?','Acknowledge the concern, explain the verified next step, and act within the applicable process.',['Ignore it because the complainant is not a personal contact.','Promise a result outside the employee’s authority.','Close the request without recording it.'],'Responsiveness calls for timely, adequate service without promising an unauthorized outcome.','gi-responsiveness','responsiveness-as-guarantee',3],
 ['cse-ethical-public-service','A staff member is asked to explain a public-service decision. Which explanation is most appropriate?','State the applicable criteria and verified facts, and identify any review route that applies.',['Rely on an undisclosed personal preference.','Claim that the decision cannot ever be reviewed.','Give a different reason to each applicant.'],'Professional and just service uses consistent criteria and an accurate account of the decision.','gi-reasons-and-review','personal-preference-as-rule',4],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Under RA 9003, which local body prepares, submits, and implements a city or municipal solid-waste management plan?','The City or Municipal Solid Waste Management Board.',['The local election board.','The national air-quality board.','A private recycling company acting alone.'],'Section 12 assigns plan preparation, submission, and implementation to the city or municipal solid-waste management board.','gi-local-plan-responsibility','plan-owner-confusion',3],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','A cleanup report counts collected litter but not waste generated or disposed through other routes. What is the main limitation?','Collection counts do not measure every waste-generation or disposal pathway.',['The collection count must be false.','All waste was necessarily collected.','The count establishes long-term system performance.'],'A collection activity records one channel and cannot stand for every pathway without further evidence.','gi-waste-measurement','single-channel-as-total',4],
 ['cse-environmental-stewardship','Which Philippine statute amended RA 9003 to institutionalize extended producer responsibility for plastic packaging?','Republic Act No. 11898.',['Republic Act No. 8749.','Republic Act No. 6713.','Republic Act No. 9003 itself.'],'RA 11898, the Extended Producer Responsibility Act of 2022, amended RA 9003 and establishes EPR obligations for covered enterprises.','republic-act-11898','amending-act-vs-original-act',3],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A facility’s emissions raise concerns about air pollution. Which statute principally addresses air-pollution prevention and control?','Republic Act No. 8749, the Philippine Clean Air Act of 1999.',['RA 9003, the solid-waste management law.','RA 6713, the public-service ethics law.','The UDHR alone.'],'RA 8749 is the Philippine Clean Air Act and addresses air-quality management and pollution control.','gi-air-quality-law','air-vs-waste-law',3],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','Readings fall after an intervention, but weather and industrial activity also change. What conclusion is warranted?','The readings fell, but the intervention’s isolated causal effect is not established.',['The intervention caused the entire change.','Weather cannot affect readings.','The observation must be discarded.'],'Concurrent factors are alternative explanations even though the measured change remains reportable.','gi-environmental-causal-limits','trend-as-cause',4],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A report compares emissions from two periods with different monitoring equipment. What should be checked before attributing a change to the environment itself?','Whether the measurement methods and coverage were comparable.',['The chart colors only.','Whether the report has a title.','Whether the newer equipment is newer.'],'A change in measurement method can affect recorded readings; comparability should be assessed.','gi-measurement-comparability','instrument-change-ignored',4],
 ['cse-public-accountability','An office publishes totals without definitions or reporting periods. What addition would make the figures more reviewable?','Define the measure, denominator where relevant, and period covered.',['Remove the source records.','Replace the totals with an unsupported conclusion.','Report only the largest value.'],'Clear definitions and periods let readers interpret and check the figures.','gi-auditability-of-reports','number-without-definition',3],
];
