 ['cse-ethical-public-service','RA 6713 directs public officials and their families to lead modest lives appropriate to their positions and income. Which norm does this describe?','Simple living.',['Political neutrality.','Justness and sincerity.','Professionalism.'],'Section 4(h) identifies simple living as a norm of conduct for public officials and employees and their families.','ra6713-simple-living','norm-confusion',3,true,null],
 ['cse-public-accountability','Under RA 6713 Section 5(e), what access does the law require for public documents?','They must be accessible and readily available for public inspection within reasonable working hours, subject to applicable legal limits.',['Every document must be released to anyone at any time, including protected personal data.','Only documents already requested by a court may be inspected.','An office may deny all inspection because the documents are held by government.'],'Section 5(e) requires access to public documents within reasonable working hours; other applicable legal protections still govern confidential material.','ra6713-public-document-access','public-access-as-unlimited',3,true,null],
 ['cse-conflict-of-interest','A manager tells an employee to approve a friend’s incomplete request “as a personal favor.” Which response best aligns with public-service ethics?','Use the published requirements consistently and raise the improper request through the proper channel.',['Approve it because the manager accepts responsibility.','Complete missing facts from memory.','Treat the request as complete to preserve the relationship.'],'Public office is a public trust; personal relationships do not replace applicable requirements.','conflict-superior-pressure','authority-as-exemption',4,true,null],
 ['cse-conflict-of-interest','An employee is asked to recommend a contractor who recently paid the employee for private consulting. What should the employee do first?','Disclose the relationship and obtain ethics guidance before making the recommendation.',['Recommend the contractor without mentioning the payment.','Recommend the contractor because the payment was for separate work.','Remove the payment from the file.'],'A recent private financial relationship may affect impartiality; the employee should not unilaterally dismiss the conflict concern.','conflict-prior-financial-relationship','separate-contract-as-no-conflict',4,true,null],

 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which option is a complete sentence rather than a dependent-clause fragment?','Although the source was incomplete, the reviewer marked the result provisional.',['Although the source was incomplete.','Because the reviewer marked the result provisional.','When the source was checked.'],'Although introduces a dependent clause that needs an independent clause; the correct option supplies both.','sentence-dependent-independent','dependent-clause-as-complete',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly joins the two independent clauses?','The totals did not match, so the clerk checked the source register.',['The totals did not match, the clerk checked the source register.','The totals did not match; because the clerk checked the source register.','The totals did not match so, the clerk checked the source register.'],'A comma plus coordinating conjunction joins the independent clauses and shows their relation.','sentence-comma-conjunction','comma-splice',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which option is a complete sentence?','After the clerk checked the entries, the supervisor released the report.',['After the clerk checked the entries.','The supervisor released the report after.','Because the entries checked by the clerk.'],'The first option has a dependent time clause and a complete main clause.','sentence-subordination','subordinate-fragment',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence avoids a run-on while preserving both findings?','The file was complete, but the reference number was incorrect.',['The file was complete the reference number was incorrect.','The file was complete, the reference number was incorrect.','The file was complete but, the reference number incorrect.'],'The comma and coordinating conjunction correctly connect two independent clauses in contrast.','sentence-run-on-repair','fused-sentence',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which revision expresses the sequence clearly in one complete sentence?','The clerk verified the code before the record was archived.',['Before the code verified.','The clerk verified before the record.','The record archived the clerk before verifying.'],'The main clause is complete and before correctly introduces the earlier action.','sentence-sequence-clause','fragmented-subordination',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Select the complete sentence with a correctly placed subordinate clause.','Because the register was unavailable, the team used the authorized duplicate.',['Because the register was unavailable, and the team used the authorized duplicate.','The team used because the register unavailable.','Because unavailable; the team used the duplicate.'],'Because introduces a dependent reason clause followed by an independent main clause.','sentence-reason-clause','conjunction-without-clause',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly uses a semicolon between related independent clauses?','The source was unavailable; the reviewer therefore marked the result provisional.',['The source was unavailable; because the reviewer marked it provisional.','The source; was unavailable, the reviewer marked it provisional.','The source was unavailable, therefore; the reviewer marked it provisional.'],'Both sides of the semicolon are independent clauses; therefore is punctuated within the second clause.','sentence-semicolon','semicolon-before-dependent-clause',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence has a complete main clause after its opening condition?','If the totals differ, the reviewer checks the underlying entries.',['If the totals differ, and the reviewer checks the entries.','If the totals differing, the reviewer checks the entries.','The reviewer checks if the totals differ, because.'],'The if-clause is dependent; the reviewer checks… supplies the independent clause.','sentence-conditional-clause','conditional-fragment',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Choose the sentence that avoids a comma splice.','The index was current, and the source register was retained.',['The index was current, the source register was retained.','The index was current; and the source register retained.','The index current, and the source register retained.'],'The conjunction joins two independent clauses; the subject and finite verb are present in each.','sentence-comma-splice-repair','comma-splice',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly coordinates a reason and a result without creating a fragment?','The source file was missing, so the reviewer requested a verified copy.',['The source file was missing, so requesting a verified copy.','The source file missing; the reviewer requested a verified copy.','Because the source file was missing, so the reviewer requested a copy.'],'So coordinates the complete reason clause with a complete result clause; because and so are not redundantly paired here.','sentence-result-coordination','double-subordinator',3,false,null],

 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A code moves each letter one place forward, with Z wrapping to A. What does “MZ” become?','NA',['NZ','MA','OB'],'M advances to N and Z wraps to A; apply the rule independently to both positions.','transform-letter-wrap','wraparound-confusion',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A four-character key is transformed by swapping only its first and fourth characters. What does “ABCD” become?','DBCA',['DCBA','ABCD','ADCB'],'The first and fourth positions exchange; the middle B and C remain fixed.','transform-endpoint-swap','reverse-entire-string',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','Under a rule, every vowel becomes the next vowel in the cycle A→E→I→O→U→A; consonants stay unchanged. What does “MAP” become?','MEP',['MIP','MUP','NAP'],'A advances to E; M and P are unchanged.','transform-vowel-cycle','change-consonants-too',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A symbol rule changes ▲ to ■, ■ to ●, and ● to ▲. What is the result of applying the rule twice to ▲?','●',['■','▲','No symbol is defined.'],'The first application gives ■; the second gives ●.','transform-two-step-map','stop-after-one-step',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A three-digit code is rotated one position to the left: 582 becomes 825. What does 731 become?','317',['173','713','137'],'Move the first digit to the end while retaining the order of the other two.','transform-left-rotation','reverse-instead-of-rotate',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A code replaces each digit d with 9−d. What does 407 become?','592',['493','507','692'],'Apply 9−d to each position: 4→5, 0→9, and 7→2.','transform-digit-complement','subtract-from-ten',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','Each letter advances three places, wrapping after Z. What does “WXY” become?','ZAB',['ZYA','ABC','XYZ'],'W→Z, X→A, and Y→B under the stated wraparound rule.','transform-multi-wrap','wrap-at-wrong-position',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A two-part code transforms by reversing the letters in each group separately: “AB-CD” becomes “BA-DC.” What is the result for “EF-GH”?','FE-HG',['HG-FE','EF-GH','FE-GH'],'Reverse each group without moving characters across the hyphen.','transform-groupwise-reversal','reverse-whole-code',3,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A rule maps 1→2, 2→4, 3→6, and 4→8. What is the output for 5?','10',['9','12','15'],'The stated mapping doubles the input.','transform-doubling-map','add-two-pattern',2,false,null],
 ['cse-abstract-transformations','A four-position code swaps positions 1 and 2 and separately swaps positions 3 and 4. What does 7614 become?','6741',['1674','7146','4167'],'The pairs are 7↔6 and 1↔4, producing 6741.','transform-adjacent-pairs','swap-only-outer-positions',3,false,null],

 ['analytical-analogy-structure','Thermometer is to temperature as odometer is to:','distance.',['direction.','weight.','time.'],'A thermometer indicates temperature; an odometer indicates distance traveled.','analogy-measurement-tool','tool-quantity-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A glossary is to word meanings as a directory is to:','contact listings.',['meeting minutes.','weather readings.','filing deadlines.'],'A glossary organizes meanings; a directory organizes contact information.','analogy-reference-resource','shared-format-not-function',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A map is to navigate as an index is to:','locate a topic or record.',['approve a transaction.','measure a quantity.','revise a sentence.'],'A map supports navigation; an index supports locating an entry.','analogy-information-tool','surface-association',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A seal is used to authenticate a document; a scale is used to:','measure weight.',['schedule a meeting.','locate a file.','authorize an employee.'],'The relation is instrument to its principal measurement or function.','analogy-instrument-function','object-category-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','An agenda organizes meeting topics; a timetable organizes:','events by time.',['documents by author.','claims by evidence.','items by price.'],'Both tools arrange information according to the dimension named in the second term.','analogy-organizing-dimension','category-match',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A sample is a subset of a population; a chapter is a subset of a:','book.',['library.','reader.','publisher.'],'Both relations are part-to-whole, with the first term contained within the second.','analogy-part-whole','subset-category-error',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A key may unlock a secured cabinet; a password may:','authenticate access to a system.',['record the system’s weight.','file a paper by surname.','measure network distance.'],'Each is a credential used to permit access to a protected resource.','analogy-access-credential','function-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','An index helps locate a record; a checksum helps:','detect certain changes in data.',['authorize a policy.','schedule a review.','translate a notice.'],'The tools have distinct functions: retrieval versus detecting data changes.','analogy-control-function','shared-domain-not-function',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','Minutes record decisions from a meeting; a receipt records:','a transaction.',['a forecast.','a sequence rule.','a word definition.'],'Both are records of an event, with the event type changed.','analogy-recorded-event','record-purpose-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['analytical-analogy-structure','A premise supports a conclusion; evidence supports an:','inference.',['appointment.','alphabetical list.','measurement unit.'],'A conclusion is drawn from premises; an inference is drawn from evidence.','analogy-reasoning-relation','association-not-relation',2,false,null],

 ['cse-number-sequence','A review schedule starts at 11 tasks and increases by 6 tasks each period. How many tasks are scheduled in period 9?','59',['54','60','65'],'The first period has 11 tasks; eight increases of 6 give 11 + 8×6 = 59.','sequence-arithmetic-position','multiply-position-without-offset',3,false,['operation'=>'sequence_arithmetic_term','start'=>11,'step'=>6,'position'=>9,'expected'=>59]],
 ['cse-number-sequence','A tracking code follows 2, 6, 18, 22, 66, 70. It alternates +4 and ×3. What follows?','210',['138','204','74'],'After the last +4, the next operation is ×3: 70 × 3 = 210.','sequence-alternating-add-multiply','repeat-additive-step',3,false,['operation'=>'sequence_pattern_next','values'=>[2,6,18,22,66,70],'rule'=>'ALTERNATING_ADD_MULTIPLY','factor'=>3,'increment'=>4,'expected'=>210]],
 ['cse-number-sequence','A set of numbered markers follows 1, 8, 27, 64. Which value follows the consecutive-cubes pattern?','125',['100','128','216'],'These are 1³, 2³, 3³, and 4³; the next is 5³ = 125.','sequence-consecutive-cubes','square-instead-of-cube',2,false,['operation'=>'sequence_pattern_next','values'=>[1,8,27,64],'rule'=>'CONSECUTIVE_CUBES','expected'=>125]],
 ['cse-number-sequence','An intended list starts at 8 and increases by 5 at every step. Which recorded value is inconsistent: 8, 13, 18, 24, 28, 33?','24',['23','28','34'],'The expected fourth value is 8 + 3×5 = 23, so 24 is the single entry that conflicts with the stated progression.','sequence-find-corrupted-entry','accept-nearby-value',3,false,['operation'=>'sequence_arithmetic_outlier','values'=>[8,13,18,24,28,33],'start'=>8,'step'=>5,'expected'=>24]],
 ['cse-number-sequence','Two interleaved sequences are 2, 3, 4, 9, 8, 27, 16, 81. What is the next term?','32',['24','64','84'],'Odd-position terms double (2, 4, 8, 16, 32); even-position terms triple (3, 9, 27, 81).','sequence-interleaved-geometric','apply-one-rule-to-all-terms',3,false,['operation'=>'sequence_pattern_next','values'=>[2,3,4,9,8,27,16,81],'rule'=>'INTERLEAVED_GEOMETRIC','expected'=>32]],

 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “For three weeks, a records unit used a checklist before accepting applications. Returned files fell from 40 to 25. During the same period, incoming applications also fell, and no comparison unit was tracked.” Which conclusion is best supported?','Returns fell while the checklist was used, but the figures do not isolate the checklist as the cause.',['The checklist alone caused every reduction.','The checklist had no effect because arrivals fell.','The unit processed more applications in total.'],'The passage reports a change during the checklist period but also identifies a competing factor and lacks a comparison unit.','reading-checklist-causal-limits','coincidence-as-causation',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “Several offices received duplicate forms. The review team proposed flagging possible duplicates at intake, then comparing correction rates for one month before expanding the process.” What is the proposal’s main logic?','Test the intake flag in a limited period and assess results before wider use.',['Reject all forms that resemble an earlier submission.','Expand the process immediately without measuring results.','Measure only how many forms arrive, not whether errors change.'],'The proposal is a bounded trial followed by measurement before expansion.','reading-pilot-before-expansion','treat-pilot-as-final-policy',3,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “At a service desk, 72 of 120 respondents said they used the online form. Respondents were invited to answer while collecting a service; residents who did not visit the desk were not surveyed.” Which inference is most careful?','The survey describes these respondents; it may not represent all residents.',['Exactly 60% of all residents use the online form.','No residents outside the desk use the online form.','The survey proves online access caused more service visits.'],'The selection method excludes people who did not visit, so generalizing to all residents is not justified.','reading-survey-sampling-frame','sample-generalization',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “Two sections tested a new filing guide. Their average retrieval time decreased from nine minutes to six, but the sections handled different document types and had no shared baseline.” What limits the comparison?','Different document types and the lack of a common baseline weaken attribution.',['The shorter time proves the guide caused the change.','The figures show that every record was retrieved in six minutes.','Averages cannot be used to compare any service process.'],'The passage names differences in case mix and baseline, so the guide’s independent effect is uncertain.','reading-pilot-comparison-limit','ignore-confounding-differences',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The notice was translated, printed in large type, and posted beside the service counter. Staff also kept copies at the entrance for visitors who preferred to read it before joining the queue.” What is the passage mainly describing?','Several ways the office made a notice easier to access.',['A rule requiring every visitor to join the queue first.','A finding that translation alone improved service speed.','A comparison of printing costs across offices.'],'The details describe format and placement choices intended to improve access, not measured effects.','reading-accessibility-main-idea','detail-mistaken-for-measured-outcome',3,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “First, the clerk checks whether each page is present. Next, the clerk records missing pages and returns the file for completion. A complete file is then sent for review.” What happens immediately before a complete file is sent for review?','The clerk checks that the pages are present.',['The reviewer returns the file for completion.','The clerk records missing pages in every file.','The file is sent back after review.'],'The described process sends a complete file onward after the completeness check; the return step applies only when pages are missing.','reading-procedure-conditional-step','apply-exception-to-all-cases',3,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The summary states that the new reminder was followed by more on-time submissions. It also notes that the reminder period coincided with a shorter application window.” Which evidence would best help assess the reminder’s contribution?','Compare similar periods or groups while accounting for the different application-window length.',['Count the number of words in the reminder.','Ask only the author whether the reminder seemed effective.','Assume every on-time submission was caused by the reminder.'],'A comparison that accounts for the changed window better separates the reminder from another relevant condition.','reading-evidence-design','ignore-alternative-explanation',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The analyst reviewed a summary table, checked two entries against the original register, and then described the result as provisional until the remaining entries were checked.” What does “provisional” signal here?','The conclusion may be revised after the remaining checks.',['The analyst has verified every entry.','The table is permanently rejected.','The original register is unnecessary.'],'The passage explicitly delays a final conclusion until verification is complete.','reading-contextual-vocabulary-provisional','treat-tentative-as-final',3,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A short report says a program reached 300 participants. It gives no information about how participants were selected, what outcomes were measured, or how long the program operated.” What can a reader reasonably conclude?','The report gives a reach count but not enough information to judge the program’s impact.',['The program improved outcomes for all 300 participants.','The program operated for exactly one year.','The participants were selected at random.'],'The passage provides a participation count and explicitly omits design and outcome details.','reading-distinguish-reach-from-impact','count-as-outcome',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “When the archive grouped files by year, staff found older records more quickly. The report cautions that the trial involved one archive room and that several staff already knew the old layout.” What is the key qualification?','The result may not generalize to other rooms or staff groups.',['Year-based grouping made every record equally easy to find.','The old layout was unknown to all staff.','The trial proves the new layout is worse.'],'The limited setting and staff familiarity constrain how broadly the finding can be applied.','reading-generalizability-qualification','ignore-scope-limitation',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The first paragraph describes a rise in incomplete applications. The second reports that most missing items were signatures or dates. The final paragraph recommends a reminder card and a later review of return rates.” Which outline best matches the passage?','Problem, observed pattern, proposed response and follow-up measure.',['Conclusion, unrelated history, and a list of staff names.','A proven solution followed by a claim that no review is needed.','A comparison of signature styles without a recommendation.'],'The sequence moves from the problem to the observed pattern, then to an action and a way to evaluate it.','reading-paragraph-organization','mistake-proposal-for-proven-result',3,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The dashboard showed that requests were completed more quickly in April. However, the office also transferred some complex requests to another unit, and the dashboard counted only requests completed locally.” What should a reader notice?','The reported speed may omit transferred complex requests.',['The dashboard necessarily counted all requests across units.','April had no complex requests.','The transfer proves local staff worked more slowly.'],'The stated measure excludes transferred requests, so the local completion figure may not reflect the full workload.','reading-measurement-scope','assume-metric-covers-all-work',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A proposal recommends sending a text reminder two days before a deadline. The author cites missed deadlines but does not report whether affected clients have reliable phone access.” Which additional information is most relevant before adopting the proposal broadly?','Whether intended recipients can reliably receive the messages, and what alternative notice is available.',['The color of the office reception chairs.','Whether the author prefers shorter reports.','The number of pages in an unrelated annual report.'],'Access to the delivery channel affects whether the intervention reaches the people it is intended to help.','reading-evaluate-implementation-assumption','ignore-access-condition',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A staff survey found that most respondents preferred the revised form. The survey was voluntary, and employees who did not use the form were not asked to respond.” What is the main limitation?','The responses may overrepresent employees who use or favor the revised form.',['The form was rejected by every respondent.','The results prove the form reduced processing time.','A voluntary survey cannot describe any respondent’s view.'],'Voluntary participation and excluding nonusers may bias the group represented.','reading-voluntary-response-bias','treat-respondents-as-all-staff',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “The pilot reduced the number of blank fields on submitted forms. The report did not measure whether the information entered in those fields was accurate.” Which conclusion is warranted?','Completeness improved on the measured fields, but accuracy was not established.',['Every newly completed field contained correct information.','Accuracy declined in every form.','The pilot had no measurable result.'],'The measured outcome concerns blank fields only; the passage says accuracy was not measured.','reading-distinguish-completeness-accuracy','equate-completion-with-correctness',4,false,null],
];
$wave4Limits=['cse-pronoun-reference'=>4,'cse-modifier-placement'=>6,'cse-parallel-structure'=>4,'cse-conflict-of-interest'=>4,'cse-public-accountability'=>3,'cse-sentence-structure'=>3,'cse-abstract-transformations'=>2,'analytical-analogy-structure'=>1,'cse-number-sequence'=>5,'cse-reading-comprehension'=>9];
$wave4Seen=[];$targetedWave4=array_values(array_filter($targetedWave4,static function(array $row)use(&$wave4Seen,$wave4Limits):bool{$concept=(string)$row[0];$wave4Seen[$concept]=($wave4Seen[$concept]??0)+1;return $wave4Seen[$concept]<=($wave4Limits[$concept]??0);}));
$environmentalWave4=[
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','Under RA 8749, what term describes the general amount of pollution in a broad area, as distinguished from discharge measurements at a source?','Ambient air quality.',['An emission measurement taken at a particular source.','A pollutant standard applied to a source.','A permit limit for an individual facility.'],'The Act distinguishes ambient air quality across a broad area from source-specific discharge or emission measurements.','gi-ambient-versus-source-measurement','source-measurement-as-area-quality',3,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A local air-quality program redesigns a process to prevent pollutants before they are released, rather than relying only on later cleanup. Which policy direction in RA 8749 does this reflect?','A primary focus on pollution prevention.',['Reliance on end-of-pipe controls as the only strategy.','Monitoring emissions without preventing pollution.','Public education without any prevention measures.'],'RA 8749 states a policy focus on pollution prevention rather than control alone.','gi-pollution-prevention-principle','control-only-after-release',3,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A monitoring report shows a significant rise in pollution and a harmful release. Which citizen-related protection does RA 8749 recognize?','Information about the nature and extent of the hazard and timely notice of significant pollution rises or harmful releases.',['Participation in formulating environmental policy.','Access to public records needed to exercise rights under the Act.','A right to bring an action concerning violations or resulting personal damages.'],'Section 4 recognizes information and timely-notice rights concerning potential hazards and significant pollution changes or releases.','gi-environmental-notice-right','notice-as-liability-finding',4,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','Residents are invited to help shape an air-quality plan and review monitoring results. Which RA 8749 principle does this implement?','Public participation in environmental policy and air-quality planning or monitoring.',['A right to timely notice of a significant pollution rise.','Access to public records needed to exercise rights under the Act.','A right to seek compensation for personal damages from an adverse impact.'],'RA 8749 recognizes citizen participation in environmental policy and programs; participation does not itself dictate the final decision.','gi-environmental-public-participation','participation-as-veto',3,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A local air-pollution problem affects one area. Which approach best reflects RA 8749’s area-based framework?','Local government addresses the problem with appropriate coordination and support under the national air-quality framework.',['Treat the national DENR framework as replacing all local action planning.','Treat the problem as solely the responsibility of individual residents.','Allow each facility to set unrelated air-quality goals.'],'The Act recognizes the area-based character of environmental responsibility and the primary responsibility of LGUs to deal with environmental problems, within the law’s coordinated framework.','gi-area-based-environmental-responsibility','local-responsibility-as-exclusive',4,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A policy assigns environmental costs to the source responsible for pollution rather than shifting them automatically to the public. Which principle named in RA 8749 is most relevant?','The “polluters must pay” principle.',['The area-based responsibility principle.','The policy of balancing development and environmental protection.','The focus on prevention rather than control alone.'],'RA 8749 expressly recognizes the polluter-pays principle.','gi-polluter-pays-principle','cost-externalization',2,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','What is one stated use of the DENR’s annual National Air Quality Status Report under RA 8749?','Inform air-quality planning using pollution trends and projections, among other information.',['Serve as the local air-quality action plan for each LGU.','Set an individual facility’s permit limit without further process.','Replace monitoring at local or airshed levels.'],'Section 6 describes the report as including current state, trends, projections, and other air-quality information used in planning.','gi-air-quality-status-report','monitoring-as-anecdote',3,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','An LGU is preparing a local air-quality action plan. What relationship to the national framework does RA 8749 describe?','The local plan should be consistent with the Integrated Air Quality Improvement Framework and developed with DENR assistance.',['The local plan replaces the Integrated Framework for the whole country.','The local plan may disregard national ambient standards.','The framework is limited to solid-waste collection.'],'RA 8749 describes LGU air-quality action planning consistent with the Integrated Framework, with DENR assistance.','gi-local-national-air-plan','local-plan-as-substitute',4,true,null],
 ['cse-environmental-public-interest','A citizen needs a public record to exercise a right recognized under the Clean Air Act. Which statement is most accurate?','RA 8749 recognizes access to relevant public records, subject to applicable legal limits.',['RA 8749 recognizes participation in policy-making but no access to relevant records.','Any record must be disclosed even if another law protects it.','Only the employee holding the record decides whether access exists.'],'Section 4 recognizes access to public records a citizen may need to exercise rights under the Act; applicable legal limitations still matter.','gi-environmental-record-access','access-as-unlimited',4,true,null],
];
$targetedWave4=array_merge($targetedWave4,$environmentalWave4);
$breadthWave4=[
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Sa pulong, iniharap ng pangkat ang isang panukala para sa bagong iskedyul. Ano ang pinakamalapit na kahulugan ng “panukala”?','mungkahi o planong isaalang-alang.',['pinal na pasiya na hindi na maaaring baguhin.','tala ng mga dumalo sa pulong.','ulat ng naganap na insidente.'],'Ang panukala ay mungkahing ihaharap para pag-usapan o isaalang-alang; hindi ito awtomatikong pinal na pasiya.','filipino-context-panukala','proposal-as-final',2,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Nasa talata ang bilang ng mga kahilingang naibalik at ang dahilan ng pagbabalik. Alin ang pinakanaaangkop na kahulugan ng “batayan” sa pangungusap na “Gamitin ang datos bilang batayan ng pagsusuri”?','salalayan o ebidensiyang pinagbabatayan ng pagsusuri.',['palamuti sa ulat.','huling hakbang ng pag-apruba.','taong nagpasya sa halip na datos.'],'Ang batayan ay impormasyong pinagsasaligan ng pagsusuri, hindi ang pasiya mismo.','filipino-context-batayan','basis-as-decision',2,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','“Tumalima ang tanggapan sa itinakdang proseso at isinumite ang tala sa tamang yunit.” Ano ang ginawa ng tanggapan?','sumunod ito sa itinakdang proseso.',['pinalitan nito ang proseso nang walang pahintulot.','tinanggihan nito ang lahat ng tala.','ipinagpaliban nito ang pagsusumite magpakailanman.'],'Ang tumalima ay sumunod o nagpasakop sa isang tuntunin o tagubilin.','filipino-context-tumalima','compliance-as-replacement',2,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Magkaiba ang petsa sa resibo at petsa sa talaan. Aling kahulugan ng “salungat” ang angkop sa pahayag na “Salungat ang dalawang petsa”?','hindi magkatugma o magkasalungat.',['magkapareho at nagtutugma.','sunod-sunod ayon sa kalendaryo.','hindi mahalaga sa pagsusuri.'],'Ipinahihiwatig ng salungat na hindi nagtutugma ang dalawang datos.','filipino-context-salungat','opposition-as-sequence',2,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Sinuri muna ng kawani ang pinagmulan ng tala bago gumawa ng konklusyon. Ano ang ipinahihiwatig ng “masusi” sa paglalarawan sa pagsusuri?','maingat at detalyado.',['mabilis ngunit walang beripikasyon.','pabigla-bigla at di-sistematikong.','paulit-ulit kahit walang layunin.'],'Ang masusing pagsusuri ay maingat at detalyado, hindi basta mabilis o padalus-dalos.','filipino-context-masusi','carefulness-as-speed',2,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','“May pahiwatig sa tala na maaaring kulang ang isang kalakip, ngunit kailangan pa itong beripikahin.” Ano ang kahulugan ng “pahiwatig” dito?','palatandaan na hindi pa tiyak na konklusyon.',['pinal na patunay na wala nang dapat suriin.','utos na itapon ang tala.','garantiya na kumpleto ang kalakip.'],'Ang pahiwatig ay palatandaan o indikasyon; hindi ito awtomatikong patunay.','filipino-context-pahiwatig','indication-as-proof',3,false,null],
 ['cse-filipino-word-usage','Sinabi sa paalala na “maaaring baguhin ang iskedyul kung may abiso.” Ano ang ipinahihiwatig ng “maaaring” sa panuto?','posible ang pagbabago kapag natugunan ang nakasaad na kondisyon.',['tiyak na binago na ang iskedyul.','bawal baguhin ang iskedyul sa lahat ng pagkakataon.','walang kaugnayan ang abiso sa pagbabago.'],'Nagpapahayag ang maaaring ng posibilidad; nililimitahan ito ng kondisyong may abiso.','filipino-modal-possibility','possibility-as-certainty',3,false,null],

 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Nagsasaad ang unang pangungusap na bumaba ang bilang ng naibalik na file. Nagsasaad ang kasunod na pangungusap na hindi nagbago ang bilang ng kulang na lagda. Aling panandang ugnayan ang angkop?','Gayunman, hindi nagbago ang bilang ng kulang na lagda.',['Samakatuwid, hindi nagbago ang bilang ng kulang na lagda.','Halimbawa, hindi nagbago ang bilang ng kulang na lagda.','Dahil dito, hindi nagbago ang bilang ng kulang na lagda.'],'Ipinakikilala ng gayunman ang pagkakaiba o limitasyong kaugnay ng naunang resulta.','cohesion-contrast-result','consequence-for-contrast',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','May pahayag na mas mabilis makuha ang mga naka-index na rekord. Aling pangungusap ang pinakamainam na sumunod bilang kongkretong halimbawa?','Sa sample na sinuri, mas maikli ang median retrieval time para sa mga file na may locator.',['Dahil dito, tiyak na lahat ng rekord ay mas mabilis nang nakukuha.','Hindi mahalaga kung may locator ang file.','Walang kailangang sukatin upang mapatunayan ang pahayag.'],'Nagbibigay ang pangungusap ng tiyak na halimbawang sumusukat sa pahayag nang hindi naglalahat sa lahat ng file.','cohesion-evidence-example','example-as-universal-proof',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Iniulat ng opisina na bumaba ang backlog matapos magbukas ng dagdag na counter. Kasabay nito, bumaba rin ang dami ng bagong kahilingan. Aling pangungusap ang pinakamainam na mag-uugnay sa dalawang katotohanan?','Gayunman, hindi maihihiwalay sa datos lamang ang epekto ng dagdag na counter sa pagbabago ng dating workload.',['Samakatuwid, dagdag na counter lamang ang sanhi ng pagbaba.','Halimbawa, walang bagong kahilingan ang natanggap kailanman.','Sa kabilang banda, imposibleng sukatin ang backlog.'],'Ang maingat na ugnayan ay naglalahad ng sabayang pagbabago nang hindi nag-aangkin ng iisang sanhi.','cohesion-concurrent-change','temporal-order-as-causation',4,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Inilista muna ng memo ang kulang na dokumento, saka ipinaliwanag kung paano ito isumite. Aling pananda ang malinaw na nagpapakilala sa susunod na hakbang?','Pagkatapos, isumite ang dokumento sa tinukoy na tanggapan.',['Gayunman, isumite ang dokumento sa tinukoy na tanggapan.','Halimbawa, isumite ang dokumento sa tinukoy na tanggapan.','Sa kabilang banda, isumite ang dokumento sa tinukoy na tanggapan.'],'Ang pagkatapos ay nagpapakita ng pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga hakbang.','cohesion-procedure-sequence','contrast-for-sequence',2,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Ipinakita ng talahanayan ang bilang ng kahilingan sa bawat yunit; hindi nito ipinakita ang laki ng populasyong pinagsisilbihan. Aling pangungusap ang angkop na kasunod?','Bukod dito, kailangan ang naaangkop na denominator bago ihambing ang dalas ng serbisyo.',['Samakatuwid, mas mahusay ang yunit na may pinakamataas na bilang.','Gayunman, hindi maaaring bilangin ang mga kahilingan.','Halimbawa, pare-pareho ang laki ng lahat ng populasyon.'],'Nagdaragdag ang bukod dito ng susunod na mahalagang limitasyon sa interpretasyon.','cohesion-additional-limitation','raw-count-as-rate',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Tumaas ang kabuuang bilang ng naasikasong kahilingan, ngunit bumaba ang bahagdan ng nakumpleto. Aling pangungusap ang pinakamalinaw na paliwanag?','Maaaring lumaki nang mas mabilis ang kabuuang bilang na pinaghahatiang batayan kaysa sa bilang ng nakumpleto.',['Hindi maaaring bumaba ang bahagdan kapag tumaas ang bilang.','Samakatuwid, maling naitala ang lahat ng bilang.','Magkapareho ang kahulugan ng kabuuan at bahagdan.'],'Magkaiba ang numerator at denominator; maaaring tumaas ang numerator habang mas mabilis lumalaki ang denominator.','cohesion-rate-explanation','count-equals-rate',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Apat na hakbang ang nasa paalala: tiyakin ang code, ihambing ang resibo, itala ang diperensiya, at isumite ang ulat. Aling pananda ang dapat magpakilala sa huling hakbang?','Sa huli, isumite ang ulat.',['Halimbawa, isumite ang ulat.','Sa kabilang banda, isumite ang ulat.','Dahil dito, isumite ang ulat.'],'Sa huli ay tumutukoy sa huling hakbang ng pagkakasunod-sunod.','cohesion-final-step','example-for-sequence',2,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Nagpapakita ang pilot ng pagbaba ng oras ng paghihintay sa dalawang linggo lamang. Aling pangungusap ang pinakaangkop na maglilimita sa konklusyon?','Gayunman, kailangan pa ng mas mahabang obserbasyon bago malaman kung nananatili ang pagbabago.',['Samakatuwid, tiyak na permanente ang pagbabago.','Bukod dito, hindi kailanman nagbabago ang oras ng paghihintay.','Halimbawa, tapos na ang lahat ng pagsubok.'],'Nililimitahan ng gayunman ang konklusyon dahil maikli pa ang panahon ng obserbasyon.','cohesion-time-limitation','short-observation-as-permanent',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Sinasabi ng ulat na “bumaba ang bilang matapos ang paalala,” ngunit walang paghahambing sa ibang panahon. Aling pagbabago ang pinakaangkop sa pahayag?','Iulat ang pagkakasabay ng pagbabago at iwasang sabihing paalala lamang ang sanhi.',['Palitan ang “matapos” ng “dahil sa” upang patunayan ang sanhi.','Alisin ang bilang dahil walang paghahambing.','Sabihing walang anumang pagbabago.'],'Ang pananalita ay dapat tumugma sa ebidensiya: temporal na pagkakasunod ay hindi sapat upang patunayan ang sanhi.','cohesion-causal-qualifier','after-as-because',4,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-cohesion','Ipinapakita ng sample na kumpleto ang karamihan sa mga file na nasuri, ngunit sample lamang ito mula sa isang sangay. Aling pangungusap ang pinakamainam na pangwakas?','Sa sangay na ito, karaniwang kumpleto ang mga file sa sample; kailangan pa ng ibang sangay upang maglahat.',['Samakatuwid, kumpleto ang lahat ng file sa buong bansa.','Hindi maaaring magbigay ng anumang paglalarawan sa sample.','Ang resulta ay patunay na pareho ang bawat sangay.'],'Tinutugma ng pangwakas ang saklaw ng pahayag sa aktuwal na pinagmulan ng sample.','cohesion-bounded-conclusion','sample-to-universal',4,false,null],

 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Naghahanda ang opisina ng maikling paalala tungkol sa pagbabalik ng kulang na aplikasyon. Aling pagkakasunod-sunod ang pinakamalinaw?','Ano ang kulang → ano ang kailangang gawin → saan at kailan ito isumite.',['Saan isusumite → hindi kaugnay na kasaysayan → ano ang kulang.','Takdang petsa → konklusyon na kumpleto ang lahat → hindi tinukoy na hakbang.','Listahan ng kawani → tuntunin → walang paliwanag sa aplikante.'],'Nagsisimula ang paalala sa suliranin, sinusundan ng kailangang aksiyon, at nagtatapos sa praktikal na detalye.','organization-action-notice','action-before-issue',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','May mga tala ang ulat tungkol sa 1) bilang ng kulang na lagda, 2) panukalang paalala, at 3) limitasyong hindi nasukat ang kawastuhan ng laman. Aling ayos ang pinakamalinaw?','Natuklasan → panukala → limitasyon sa ebidensiya.',['Limitasyon → panukala → hindi kaugnay na natuklasan.','Panukala bilang napatunayang resulta → natuklasan → alisin ang limitasyon.','Listahan ng tala → konklusyon na walang batayan → panukala.'],'Ipinakikita muna ang batayang problema bago ang tugon at nililinaw pagkatapos kung ano ang hindi pa napatutunayan.','organization-finding-response-limit','proposal-as-finding',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Aling pangungusap ang pinakamainam na pambungad sa talatang nagpapaliwanag kung bakit nagkulang ang ulat sa paghahambing?','Gumamit ang dalawang tanggapan ng magkaibang depinisyon ng “nakumpleto,” kaya hindi direktang maihahambing ang kanilang bilang.',['Dahil dito, tiyak na mas mahusay ang unang tanggapan.','Nang sumunod na buwan, nagpalit ng kulay ang pabalat ng ulat.','Ang konklusyon ay dapat ilagay bago tukuyin ang mga sukatan.'],'Ipinakikilala ng unang pangungusap ang suliraning lohikal na susundan ng paliwanag at kinakailangang limitasyon.','organization-topic-sentence','conclusion-before-issue',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Naglalaman ang isang talata ng pahayag tungkol sa bilis ng proseso, datos ng median, at limitasyong hindi kasama ang mga hindi kumpletong aplikasyon. Aling detalye ang hindi dapat alisin sa konklusyon?','Na hindi inilalarawan ng median ang mga aplikasyong hindi isinama sa sukatan.',['Pamagat ng talahanayan lamang.','Pangalan ng encoder na nag-type ng bilang.','Kulay ng mga kahon sa grap.'],'Nililimitahan ng ibinukod na grupo ang saklaw ng konklusyon at mahalaga ito sa interpretasyon.','organization-relevant-limitation','omit-denominator-boundary',4,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Aling pagkakasunod-sunod ang sumusunod sa proseso ng pagtanggap ng dokumento?','Tiyakin ang mga pahina → itala ang kakulangan kung mayroon → ibalik para makumpleto o ipadala sa pagsusuri kung kumpleto.',['Ipadala sa pagsusuri → saka bilangin ang pahina → magpasya kung may dokumento.','Ibalik ang lahat ng file → huwag itala ang dahilan → tiyakin ang pahina.','Itala ang kakulangan bago tingnan ang dokumento → ipadala lahat sa pagsusuri.'],'Nagsisimula ang proseso sa beripikasyon at nagkakaiba ang susunod na hakbang depende kung kumpleto ang file.','organization-conditional-process','conditional-step-before-check',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','May konklusyong nagsasabing epektibo ang bagong paalala batay sa pagbaba ng balik na aplikasyon sa isang linggo. Ano ang pinakamainam na rebisyon sa konklusyon?','Sabihing bumaba ang naibalik na aplikasyon sa naobserbahang linggo; kailangan pa ng paghahambing upang matukoy ang sanhi.',['Sabihing napatunayan na ang pangmatagalang epekto sa lahat ng tanggapan.','Alisin ang naobserbahang bilang at magbigay ng tiyak na garantiya.','Ipahayag na walang pagbabago kahit bumaba ang bilang.'],'Nananatili ang naiulat na obserbasyon ngunit nililimitahan ang sanhi at lawak ng pahayag.','organization-revise-overclaim','observation-to-causation',4,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Nais ihambing ng ulat ang pagdami ng kahilingan at ang pagbaba ng completion rate. Aling ayos ng paliwanag ang pinakamalinaw?','Ilarawan ang dalawang sukatan, tukuyin ang denominator ng rate, saka ipaliwanag kung paano maaaring magkaiba ang direksiyon ng mga ito.',['Sabihing pareho ang kahulugan ng count at rate, saka laktawan ang base.','Ibigay ang konklusyon bago banggitin ang alinmang datos.','Ihambing lamang ang kabuuang bilang at ipalagay na iyon ang rate.'],'Kailangan munang tukuyin ang dalawang sukatan at denominator bago ipaliwanag ang magkaibang galaw.','organization-count-rate-explanation','rate-without-denominator',4,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Aling pangungusap ang pinakamainam na sumunod sa pahayag na “Bumaba ang average na oras, ngunit hindi isinama ang mga kasong kulang ang source record”?','Samakatuwid, naaangkop lamang ang rate sa mga kasong kasama sa pagsusuri.',['Dahil dito, bumilis ang bawat kaso.','Halimbawa, walang source record na kulang.','Sa kabilang banda, dapat balewalain ang denominator.'],'Ipinapaliwanag ng pangungusap ang limitasyong tuwirang sumusunod sa nakasaad na exclusion.','organization-denominator-caveat','excluded-cases-as-included',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','May tatlong pangungusap: A) “Kailangan pang beripikahin ang resulta.” B) “Tumaas ang bilang sa unang linggo.” C) “Hindi pa kasama ang ikalawang sangay.” Aling ayos ang pinakamalinaw para sa maikling ulat?','B → C → A.',['A → A → B.','C → A → B.','B → A → C.'],'Inilalahad muna ang obserbasyon, kasunod ang limitasyong may kinalaman sa saklaw, at pagkatapos ang nararapat na maingat na konklusyon.','organization-observation-scope-conclusion','conclusion-before-evidence',3,false,null],
 ['cse-paragraph-organization','Aling detalye ang dapat manatili sa talatang nagtataya kung nabawasan ang error sa pag-file?','Bilang ng error bago at pagkatapos, magkatulad na panahon, at depinisyon ng error.',['Laki ng font sa pabalat lamang.','Hindi kaugnay na iskedyul ng pagpupulong.','Pangalan ng taong nag-print ng ulat.'],'Kailangan ang maihahambing na sukat at depinisyon upang masuportahan ang pagtataya.','organization-measurement-evidence','decorative-detail-as-evidence',3,false,null],

 ['cse-sentence-completion','The list of required attachments, including the signed form, ___ in the notice.','appears',['appear','are appearing tomorrow','have appear'],'The head noun list is singular; the intervening phrase does not change the subject.','completion-singular-head','intervening-plural-controls',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','After the reviewer ___ the source entries, the office released the corrected table.','checked',['checking','checks yesterday','had check'],'The completed past action checked fits the time sequence and the clause structure.','completion-past-sequence','tense-form-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The figures are not directly comparable ___ the two offices used different definitions.','because',['nevertheless','for example','similarly'],'Because introduces the reason that explains why the figures cannot be compared directly.','completion-causal-connector','contrast-for-cause',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','Neither option ___ the requirement that every copy include a date and reference code.','meets',['meet','are meeting yesterday','have met tomorrow'],'Neither option is singular in this construction, so the singular verb meets is appropriate.','completion-neither-agreement','plural-near-noun-controls',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The office will archive the report ___ the authorized reviewer signs the final copy.','after',['although','unless of','despite that'],'After introduces the time condition for archiving the report.','completion-time-clause','concession-for-sequence',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The analyst compared the count with the rate, ___ the two measures use different denominators.','although',['therefore','for instance','as a result of'],'Although introduces a qualification that contrasts the comparison with the denominator difference.','completion-concession','consequence-for-concession',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The committee asked the two offices to submit ___ revised definitions before the comparison.','their',['there','they’re','its'],'Their is the possessive determiner referring to the two offices.','completion-possessive-reference','there-their-theyre',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','If the original record is unavailable, the reviewer ___ the result as provisional until verification is complete.','marks',['marked tomorrow','marking','have marked'],'The present-tense conditional pairs if the record is unavailable with the main-clause verb marks.','completion-conditional-agreement','conditional-verb-form',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-completion','The procedure requires checking the identifier, comparing the date, and ___ the source of any discrepancy.','documenting',['to document','documentation','the source is documented'],'The three coordinated items are gerund phrases governed by requires.','completion-parallel-gerunds','mixed-list-form',2,false,null],

 ['cse-grammar-application','Choose the clearest standard sentence: “The amount of pending work vary by week.”','The amount of pending work varies by week.',['The amount of pending work vary by weeks.','The amount of pending work are varying by week.','Pending work, the amount vary by week.'],'The grammatical head is singular amount, so the verb is varies; work is an uncountable noun here.','grammar-head-amount-agreement','nearest-plural-controls',2,false,null],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Which revision correctly punctuates the sentence? “The file was complete however the index lacked a date.”','The file was complete; however, the index lacked a date.',['The file was complete, however the index lacked a date.','The file was complete; however the index, lacked a date.','The file was complete however; the index lacked a date.'],'However connects two independent clauses as a conjunctive adverb; use a semicolon before it and a comma after it.','error-recognition-conjunctive-adverb','comma-splice-however',3,false,null],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Select the sentence with the correct possessive form.','The reviewers checked their notes before submitting them.',['The reviewers checked there notes before submitting them.','The reviewers checked they’re notes before submitting them.','The reviewers checked its notes before submitting them.'],'Their is the possessive determiner for the plural reviewers; there is locative and they’re means they are.','error-recognition-their','homophone-confusion',2,false,null],
 ['cse-error-recognition','Which revision removes the misplaced modifier? “The office returned the application to the applicant with a missing signature.”','The office returned the application with the missing signature to the applicant.',['The office with a missing signature returned the application to the applicant.','The office returned the application to the applicant, who had a missing signature.','With a missing signature, the office returned the applicant the application.'],'The revised placement attaches the missing-signature description to application rather than office or applicant.','error-recognition-modifier-attachment','modifier-nearest-noun',3,false,null],
 ['cse-word-meaning','The auditor described the estimate as “tentative” until the source records were checked. Tentative most nearly means:','provisional and subject to change.',['final and binding.','unrelated to the source records.','deliberately inaccurate.'],'The source review is unfinished, so tentative means not yet final and potentially changeable.','vocabulary-tentative-context','tentative-as-false',2,false,null],

 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly joins two independent clauses without a conjunctive adverb?','The source register was unavailable; the reviewer marked the result provisional.',['The source register; was unavailable and the result provisional.','The source register was unavailable; because the result was provisional.','The source register was unavailable,; the reviewer marked the result provisional.'],'The semicolon separates two closely related independent clauses; because introduces a dependent clause, and the other choices misuse clause punctuation.','sentence-structure-semicolon','semicolon-before-dependent-clause',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which revision repairs the run-on without changing the two reported actions?','The clerk checked the total, and the reviewer verified the source.',['The clerk checked the total the reviewer verified the source.','The clerk checked the total, the reviewer verified the source.','The clerk checked; the total and reviewer verified the source.'],'A comma and coordinating conjunction join the two complete clauses.','sentence-structure-run-on','fused-clause',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which choice contains both an introductory dependent clause and a complete main clause?','Although the count increased, the rate declined.',['Although the count increased.','Because the denominator grew faster.','While the figures were being compared.'],'Although introduces a dependent clause; the main clause the rate declined completes the sentence.','sentence-structure-subordination','dependent-fragment',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence clearly identifies the actor who checked the receipt?','After the clerk checked the receipt, the analyst recorded the result.',['After checking the receipt, the result was recorded by the analyst.','After the receipt was checked, recording the result.','The receipt checked the analyst after the result.'],'The first clause names the clerk as the person who checked the receipt, and the main clause names the analyst’s action.','sentence-structure-actor-clarity','dangling-opening-clause',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly places the condition and result?','If the source total differs, the reviewer checks the underlying entries.',['If the source total differs, and the reviewer checks the entries.','The reviewer checks the entries if differs the source total.','If the source total differing; the reviewer checks the entries.'],'The if-clause is dependent and is followed by a complete main clause.','sentence-structure-condition-result','conditional-fragment',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Choose the clearest sentence combining the two facts: the form was incomplete; the clerk returned it.','Because the form was incomplete, the clerk returned it.',['Because the form was incomplete, and the clerk returned it.','The form was incomplete, the clerk returned it.','The clerk returned because the form incomplete it.'],'Because introduces a reason clause and the main clause states the result.','sentence-structure-cause-combination','double-conjunction',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence avoids an incomplete comparison?','The revised checklist is clearer than the earlier version.',['The revised checklist is clearer than the earlier version is clear.','The revised checklist is clearer than reviewing the earlier version.','The revised checklist is clearer compared than before.'],'The comparison matches checklist with checklist and states the intended basis.','sentence-structure-comparison','unmatched-comparison',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence correctly coordinates the two independent clauses?','The file lacked a page, so the clerk requested a complete copy.',['The file lacked a page, the clerk requested a complete copy.','The file lacked a page; because the clerk requested a copy.','The file lacked a page so, the clerk requested a complete copy.'],'The comma plus coordinating conjunction so joins the complete reason and result clauses.','sentence-structure-coordination','comma-splice',2,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which option makes the scope of “only” clear?','The clerk checked only the date field.',['Only the clerk checked the date field.','The clerk only checked the date field after lunch.','The clerk checked the date field only after lunch.'],'Only immediately precedes date field, the element intended to be restricted.','sentence-structure-limiting-word','only-scope-shift',3,false,null],
 ['cse-sentence-structure','Which sentence combines the observation and limitation without claiming an unsupported cause?','Returns fell during the pilot, although incoming applications also declined.',['Returns fell because of the pilot, and incoming applications also declined.','The pilot caused every change despite the missing comparison.','Incoming applications declined; therefore returns could not have changed.'],'During reports timing; although preserves the concurrent change as a limitation rather than asserting causation.','sentence-structure-qualified-observation','concurrent-change-as-proof',4,false,null],

 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A service unit reported that median waiting time fell from 28 minutes to 21 minutes. It also changed the way it recorded walk-in cases during the second period.” What should a reader check before interpreting the difference?','Whether the changed recording method makes the two periods comparable.',['Whether the median can ever be calculated.','Whether every visitor waited exactly 21 minutes.','Whether the first period had no walk-in cases.'],'A change in measurement or inclusion can affect comparability even when both medians are calculated correctly.','reading-measurement-change','measurement-change-ignored',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “In a trial, 18 of 24 users completed an online form without assistance. The trial took place at a branch with reliable public Wi-Fi, and no offline users were included.” What is the most careful conclusion?','The result describes the trial participants; access conditions may differ elsewhere.',['Exactly 75% of all residents can complete the form.','The form works equally well without internet access.','The trial proves every branch should discontinue in-person assistance.'],'The sample and setting limit generalization to users and branches with different access conditions.','reading-technology-access-limit','local-result-as-universal',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A memo says that 90% of requests were resolved within five days. It excludes requests awaiting documents from applicants and does not report their number.” What is the main limitation?','The reported rate does not describe the excluded requests or their share of all requests.',['The 90% figure proves every request was completed.','The excluded requests must all have been resolved within five days.','A rate can never be reported when any request is excluded.'],'The exclusion changes the population described, and the missing count prevents judging its size.','reading-exclusion-size','excluded-subgroup-as-zero',4,false,null],
 ['cse-reading-comprehension','Read the passage: “A weekly report showed 44, 51, and 49 resolved cases. The report gives no staffing levels, incoming workload, or comparison with another unit.” Which statement is warranted?','The reported values rose and then fell; the series alone does not identify why.',['A staffing change caused the rise.','The next week will necessarily contain fewer than 49 cases.','All units followed the same pattern.'],'The three observations support a description of the sequence, not an explanation or forecast.','reading-descriptive-series','trend-as-cause-or-forecast',3,false,null],

 ['cse-civic-participation','An agency invites residents to comment on a draft plan before final approval. What does that timing allow?','Input can inform the decision while options are still under consideration.',['Every submitted comment must be adopted.','The consultation replaces the agency’s legal decision process.','Comments received before approval are automatically binding.'],'Consultation before finalization can inform deliberation, but does not by itself dictate the outcome.','civic-input-before-decision','consultation-as-veto',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A meeting records 80 comments from one neighborhood, while two other affected neighborhoods were not reached. What is the best description of the record?','It documents the views received but does not establish that they represent every affected neighborhood.',['It proves all residents agree with the comments.','The unrepresented neighborhoods have no relevant views.','The number of comments determines the final policy.'],'A count of submissions describes participation received, not representativeness of groups that were not reached.','civic-comment-count-scope','volume-as-representativeness',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A consultation notice is posted one day before a meeting, although the affected groups need time to review technical documents. What should the agency assess?','Whether the notice and access to materials provide a meaningful opportunity to participate.',['Whether posting any notice automatically proves meaningful access.','Whether affected groups should be excluded from technical topics.','Whether comments must change the proposal to count.'],'Meaningful participation depends on usable notice and opportunity, not publication alone.','civic-notice-opportunity','publication-as-access',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','After a consultation, a public office publishes the comments received and explains which issues changed the draft and why others did not. What does this most directly support?','A reviewable account of how public input was considered.',['A guarantee that every commenter agrees with the result.','Proof that comments determined every final provision.','A rule that the proposal cannot be revised again.'],'Documenting disposition makes the consideration process more transparent without treating input as a binding vote.','civic-comment-disposition','input-as-binding-result',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An in-person hearing is held in a location difficult to reach for residents affected by the proposal. What is a useful next step?','Consider accessible ways for those residents to receive information and provide input.',['Assume nonattendance means consent.','Treat the attendance list as a complete measure of public opinion.','Close other channels so every view is collected in one place.'],'Access barriers may affect who participates; additional channels can make the process more inclusive.','civic-participation-barrier','nonattendance-as-consent',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A poll of meeting attendees favors one option, but attendance was voluntary and no sampling method was used. What may be said?','The result describes the attendees who responded, not necessarily the wider population.',['The poll establishes the preference of every affected resident.','Voluntary participation guarantees a representative sample.','The poll proves the other option has no support.'],'Self-selection limits how confidently the result can represent people who did not attend or respond.','civic-self-selected-poll','attendees-as-population',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','A consultation accepts both written submissions and oral comments, then records them using the same published criteria. What is the strongest procedural benefit?','Different participation channels can be considered consistently under a transparent process.',['Every channel guarantees identical participation rates.','Using two channels makes evaluation unnecessary.','Oral comments must always outweigh written evidence.'],'Multiple channels can broaden access; consistent criteria help make consideration reviewable.','civic-multiple-channel-review','channel-as-guarantee',3,false,null],
 ['cse-civic-participation','An office receives no comments on a draft policy from people who were not reached by its notice. What should it avoid inferring?','That nonresponse proves those people support the draft.',['That no comments were recorded through the notice.','That the notice may not have reached everyone.','That further outreach could be considered.'],'Silence among people not reached is not evidence of agreement.','civic-nonresponse-interpretation','silence-as-consent',3,false,null],

 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A public agency requires applicants for an ordinary civil benefit to profess a particular religion, without a lawful constitutional basis. Which principle is most directly implicated?','The constitutional protection of religious freedom and prohibition on a religious test for civil or political rights.',['A rule that every applicant must share the same belief.','A guarantee that no generally applicable law may apply to religious conduct.','A right to select the employee who processes the application.'],'Article III protects free exercise and provides that no religious test shall be required for the exercise of civil or political rights.','rights-religious-test','religion-as-qualification',3,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','Employees form a peaceful association to discuss workplace concerns. Which general constitutional protection is relevant?','The right to form associations or societies for purposes not contrary to law.',['A requirement that every employee join the association.','A guarantee that the association’s proposals must be adopted.','A right to disregard every lawful workplace rule.'],'Article III, Section 8 protects the right to form associations or societies for purposes not contrary to law.','rights-association','association-as-compulsion',3,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A person is publicly accused of an offense, but no court has decided the case. Which principle should guide an official description of the person?','Do not describe guilt as established solely from the accusation; the accused is presumed innocent until proven otherwise.',['An accusation itself proves guilt.','The person may never be investigated.','The complainant’s statement is automatically a final judgment.'],'Article III, Section 14(2) states the presumption of innocence in criminal prosecutions.','rights-presumption-innocence','accusation-as-judgment',3,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A government office bars peaceful criticism of a policy solely because the speaker disagrees with the office. Which general protection is implicated?','Freedom of speech and expression, subject to applicable constitutional limits.',['A guarantee that criticism must change the policy.','An unlimited right to disrupt every public service.','A rule that only supportive views may be expressed.'],'Article III, Section 4 protects speech and expression; the facts do not establish a basis for viewpoint-based suppression.','rights-peaceful-expression','right-as-guaranteed-outcome',3,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A rule applies a classification to similarly situated people. What question is central to an equal-protection review?','Whether the classification has a lawful and reasonable basis and is applied consistently under the governing standard.',['Whether every person has identical circumstances.','Whether the rule was printed in the same font.','Whether the classification is convenient for the office alone.'],'Equal protection does not require identical treatment in every circumstance; the classification must satisfy the applicable legal standard.','rights-equal-protection-classification','uniformity-as-equality',4,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','A person in a criminal prosecution asks for a speedy, impartial, and public trial. Which constitutional guarantee is most directly relevant?','The rights of the accused in criminal prosecutions under Article III, Section 14.',['A guarantee that every hearing must be held in a private home.','A rule that a trial ends as soon as a request is filed.','A right to choose the judge after proceedings begin.'],'Section 14(2) includes the right to a speedy, impartial, and public trial, subject to the Constitution’s stated rules.','rights-trial-guarantee','speedy-as-immediate',3,false,null],
 ['cse-human-rights-dignity','An office collects sensitive personal details that are not needed to decide an application. Which rights-based concern should it examine?','Whether the collection has a lawful, relevant purpose and respects applicable privacy safeguards.',['Whether collecting more personal data is always better.','Whether the information should be published to prove transparency.','Whether privacy matters only after information is disclosed.'],'Purpose and necessity matter when handling personal information; the collection should not exceed lawful needs.','rights-privacy-purpose','more-data-as-better',3,false,null],

